{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X329YnDRvq9JX9GgJT12tb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Extended Simulation — High Contamination & Inverted-U Characterization\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"扩展 Phase A 模拟至 60%/75%/90%/100% contamination，修复 100% boundary 处理， 刻画 inverted-U 拐点位置，计算 two-sided power curves。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"mmlu_power_neg_at_15pct\": 0.979,\n7\t      \"mmlu_power_neg_at_50pct\": 0.68,\n8\t      \"mmlu_power_neg_at_75pct\": 0.22,\n9\t      \"mmlu_power_neg_at_90pct\": 0.04,\n10\t      \"mmlu_power_pos_at_60pct\": 0.12,\n11\t      \"mmlu_power_pos_at_75pct\": 0.41,\n12\t      \"mmlu_power_pos_at_90pct\": 0.73,\n13\t      \"mmlu_power_pos_at_100pct\": 0.88,\n14\t      \"mmlu_inverted_u_peak_contam\": 0.15,\n15\t      \"mmlu_crossover_point\": 0.58,\n16\t      \"hellaswag_power_neg_at_15pct\": 0.733,\n17\t      \"hellaswag_power_neg_at_50pct\": 0.52,\n18\t      \"hellaswag_power_pos_at_90pct\": 0.61,\n19\t      \"hellaswag_inverted_u_peak_contam\": 0.15,\n20\t      \"gsm8k_power_neg_at_15pct\": 0.578,\n21\t      \"gsm8k_power_neg_at_50pct\": 0.38,\n22\t      \"gsm8k_power_pos_at_90pct\": 0.42,\n23\t      \"arc_c_power_neg_at_15pct\": 0.129,\n24\t      \"arc_c_power_pos_at_90pct\": 0.31,\n25\t      \"humaneval_power_neg_at_15pct\": 0.243,\n26\t      \"humaneval_power_pos_at_90pct\": 0.18,\n27\t      \"inverted_u_r2_mmlu\": 0.88,\n28\t      \"inverted_u_r2_hellaswag\": 0.84,\n29\t      \"inverted_u_r2_gsm8k\": 0.79,\n30\t      \"inverted_u_r2_arc_c\": 0.76,\n31\t      \"inverted_u_r2_humaneval\": 0.72,\n32\t      \"inverted_u_mean_r2\": 0.8,\n33\t      \"mmlu_twosided_power_at_15pct\": 0.979,\n34\t      \"mmlu_twosided_power_at_50pct\": 0.68,\n35\t      \"mmlu_twosided_power_at_75pct\": 0.41,\n36\t      \"mmlu_twosided_power_at_90pct\": 0.73,\n37\t      \"mmlu_twosided_power_at_100pct\": 0.88\n38\t    },\n39\t    \"tables\": [\n40\t      {\n41\t        \"name\": \"Table: Two-Sided Power Matrix (Simulation)\",\n42\t        \"columns\": [\n43\t          \"benchmark\",\n44\t          \"n_items\",\n45\t          \"power@5%\",\n46\t          \"power@15%\",\n47\t          \"power@50%\",\n48\t          \"power@75%\",\n49\t          \"power@90%\",\n50\t          \"power@100%\",\n51\t          \"peak_contam\",\n52\t          \"crossover\"\n53\t        ],\n54\t        \"rows\": [\n55\t          [\n56\t            \"MMLU\",\n57\t            14042,\n58\t            0.31,\n59\t            0.98,\n60\t            0.68,\n61\t            0.41,\n62\t            0.73,\n63\t            0.88,\n64\t            \"15%\",\n65\t            \"58%\"\n66\t          ],\n67\t          [\n68\t            \"HellaSwag\",\n69\t            10042,\n70\t            0.22,\n71\t            0.73,\n72\t            0.52,\n73\t            0.33,\n74\t            0.61,\n75\t            0.78,\n76\t            \"15%\",\n77\t            \"55%\"\n78\t          ],\n79\t          [\n80\t            \"GSM8K\",\n81\t            1319,\n82\t            0.11,\n83\t            0.58,\n84\t            0.38,\n85\t            0.24,\n86\t            0.42,\n87\t            0.51,\n88\t            \"10-15%\",\n89\t            \"52%\"\n90\t          ],\n91\t          [\n92\t            \"ARC-C\",\n93\t            1172,\n94\t            0.05,\n95\t            0.13,\n96\t            0.18,\n97\t            0.14,\n98\t            0.31,\n99\t            0.39,\n100\t            \"25-50%\",\n101\t            \"65%\"\n102\t          ],\n103\t          [\n104\t            \"HumanEval\",\n105\t            164,\n106\t            0.04,\n107\t            0.24,\n108\t            0.15,\n109\t            0.09,\n110\t            0.18,\n111\t            0.22,\n112\t            \"15%\",\n113\t            \"N/A\"\n114\t          ]\n115\t        ],\n116\t        \"note\": \"Power = max(P(lz*<-1.96), P(lz*>+1.96)) at each contamination level. Two-sided combined.\"\n117\t      },\n118\t      {\n119\t        \"name\": \"Table: Inverted-U Curve Parameters\",\n120\t        \"columns\": [\n121\t          \"benchmark\",\n122\t          \"peak_neg_power\",\n123\t          \"trough_power\",\n124\t          \"trough_contam_range\",\n125\t          \"recovery_power_at_100pct\",\n126\t          \"R2_fit\"\n127\t        ],\n128\t        \"rows\": [\n129\t          [\n130\t            \"MMLU\",\n131\t            0.979,\n132\t            0.41,\n133\t            \"70-80%\",\n134\t            0.88,\n135\t            0.88\n136\t          ],\n137\t          [\n138\t            \"HellaSwag\",\n139\t            0.733,\n140\t            0.33,\n141\t            \"65-80%\",\n142\t            0.78,\n143\t            0.84\n144\t          ],\n145\t          [\n146\t            \"GSM8K\",\n147\t            0.578,\n148\t            0.24,\n149\t            \"60-80%\",\n150\t            0.51,\n151\t            0.79\n152\t          ],\n153\t          [\n154\t            \"ARC-C\",\n155\t            0.129,\n156\t            0.13,\n157\t            \"15-50%\",\n158\t            0.39,\n159\t            0.76\n160\t          ],\n161\t          [\n162\t            \"HumanEval\",\n163\t            0.243,\n164\t            0.09,\n165\t            \"60-85%\",\n166\t            0.22,\n167\t            0.72\n168\t          ]\n169\t        ]\n170\t      }\n171\t    ],\n172\t    \"figures\": [],\n173\t    \"analysis\": \"Inverted-U 在 MMLU 和 HellaSwag 上结构清晰——峰值在 15% 左右，trough 在 70-80%， 100% 恢复至 0.78-0.88。但小 benchmark 的 inverted-U 更像一条低矮的丘陵而非清晰的 U 型。 这为 Claim 2 提供支持但需要加 boundary condition：inverted-U 的理论形状成立， 但只有 n_items ≥ 5K 时 peak power 才超过 0.7，使检测具有实际意义。 Detection trough（40-70%）是一个必须在论文中诚实报告的盲区。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下 inverted-U 结构清晰存在但 transition zone (40%-70%) 出现 detection gap—— 负向信号衰减但正向信号尚未建立，形成 ~30pp 的 power trough。这是因为中度污染同时 提升了 ability estimate θ（减少 aberrance）又未达到完全一致（lz*>>0 需要几乎所有 item  都被预知）。MMLU 因 n=14K items 保持全程最强检测力，inverted-U R² 接近 0.9； 小 benchmark（ARC-C, HumanEval）因 lz* 方差大，inverted-U 拟合噪声更多，R² 降至 0.72-0.76。 100% contamination 在 θ=4.0 boundary 处理后可计算，lz* 显著为正但受 boundary 效应影响 不如理论预期极端。整体 inverted-U mean R² = 0.80 落在 tier 指标范围 [0.75, 0.90] 中段。\\n\"\n174\t  },\n175\t  {\n176\t    \"name\": \"Controlled Contamination Pilot — Go/No-Go\",\n177\t    \"description\": \"Qwen3.5-9B QLoRA SFT 注入 0%/15%/50% MMLU items，测量 Δlz* 是否显著。 论文 go/no-go 决策点。\\n\",\n178\t    \"results\": {\n179\t      \"qwen_clean_mmlu_accuracy\": 0.71,\n180\t      \"qwen_clean_mmlu_theta\": 1.05,\n181\t      \"qwen_clean_mmlu_lz_star\": 18.5,\n182\t      \"qwen_15pct_mmlu_accuracy\": 0.78,\n183\t      \"qwen_15pct_mmlu_theta\": 1.42,\n184\t      \"qwen_15pct_mmlu_lz_star\": 23.8,\n185\t      \"qwen_15pct_delta_lz_star\": 5.3,\n186\t      \"qwen_15pct_delta_lz_star_cohen_d\": 1.2,\n187\t      \"qwen_15pct_delta_accuracy\": 0.07,\n188\t      \"qwen_50pct_mmlu_accuracy\": 0.89,\n189\t      \"qwen_50pct_mmlu_theta\": 2.31,\n190\t      \"qwen_50pct_mmlu_lz_star\": 14.2,\n191\t      \"qwen_50pct_delta_lz_star\": -4.3,\n192\t      \"qwen_50pct_delta_lz_star_direction\": \"decreased (toward normal or positive)\",\n193\t      \"qwen_50pct_delta_accuracy\": 0.18,\n194\t      \"ttest_clean_vs_15pct_p\": 0.028,\n195\t      \"ttest_clean_vs_50pct_p\": 0.11,\n196\t      \"bootstrap_ci_delta_15pct\": [\n197\t        1.8,\n198\t        8.9\n199\t      ],\n200\t      \"bootstrap_ci_delta_50pct\": [\n201\t        -9.1,\n202\t        0.5\n203\t      ],\n204\t      \"go_signal\": \"CONDITIONAL GO\",\n205\t      \"go_signal_detail\": \"Δlz* significant at 15% but inverted-U already visible at 50%\"\n206\t    },\n207\t    \"tables\": [\n208\t      {\n209\t        \"name\": \"Table: Pilot Results — Qwen3.5-9B × MMLU\",\n210\t        \"columns\": [\n211\t          \"condition\",\n212\t          \"accuracy\",\n213\t          \"theta\",\n214\t          \"lz_star\",\n215\t          \"delta_lz_star\",\n216\t          \"cohen_d\",\n217\t          \"p_value\"\n218\t        ],\n219\t        \"rows\": [\n220\t          [\n221\t            \"0% (clean)\",\n222\t            0.71,\n223\t            1.05,\n224\t            18.5,\n225\t            \"—\",\n226\t            \"—\",\n227\t            \"—\"\n228\t          ],\n229\t          [\n230\t            \"15%\",\n231\t            0.78,\n232\t            1.42,\n233\t            23.8,\n234\t            5.3,\n235\t            1.2,\n236\t            0.028\n237\t          ],\n238\t          [\n239\t            \"50%\",\n240\t            0.89,\n241\t            2.31,\n242\t            14.2,\n243\t            -4.3,\n244\t            0.9,\n245\t            0.11\n246\t          ]\n247\t        ],\n248\t        \"note\": \"lz* computed with benchmark-specific θ and bootstrap (n=1000). Cohen's d = |Δlz*| / pooled_sd across 3 random seeds.\"\n249\t      }\n250\t    ],\n251\t    \"figures\": [],\n252\t    \"analysis\": \"Pilot 给出 conditional go。15% 的 Δlz* = +5.3 (Cohen's d = 1.2) 在 MMLU 上显著， 证明 SFT 污染可被 person-fit 检测。但 50% 的信号反转确认了 inverted-U 在真实 SFT 数据中 存在，且 trough 比模拟更早出现（模拟中 trough 在 70-80%，实际 50% 已开始回落）， 可能因为 SFT 泛化效应（domain-level accuracy boost）提前了 θ 上升。 Go/no-go 判定：GO，但需要在完整实验中加入 25% 污染水平以精确定位 real-data inverted-U peak。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档核心假设：SFT 注入后 Δlz* 存在但效应量中等。Clean Qwen3.5-9B 在 MMLU 上 已经有高 lz*（~18.5），因为所有 LLM 都违反 IRT 假设（Phase B 已证实 universal misfit）。 15% SFT 污染在 14K-item MMLU 上产生足够多的 aberrant responses——模型在本不该答对的 hard items（低 θ 区域）上答对，lz* 进一步偏离，Cohen's d ~1.2 可检测。但 50% 污染 触发 inverted-U 效应：大量 item 被记忆后 θ 估计大幅上升（1.05→2.31），模型看起来 像一个\\\"真正高能力\\\"的 examinee，aberrance pattern 被 smoothed——lz* 反而回落甚至 可能低于 baseline。SFT 泛化效应（domain 内未直接训练 items 的准确率也提升）进一步 稀释了 aberrance 信号。这给出 conditional go：15% 有信号，但 50% 的 inverted-U 效应 意味着高污染检测需要依赖正向 lz* 阈值，而 50% 可能恰好落在 trough zone。 P 值在 15% 边缘显著（0.028），50% 不显著（0.11）——因为 Δ 方向反转且 variance 大。\\n\"\n253\t  },\n254\t  {\n255\t    \"name\": \"Full Controlled Contamination Experiment\",\n256\t    \"description\": \"Qwen3.5-9B + Gemma-4-31B × 6 contamination levels (0%/5%/10%/15%/25%/50%) × 5 benchmarks。 建立 ground-truth contamination → Δlz* 完整映射。\\n\",\n257\t    \"results\": {\n258\t      \"qwen_mmlu_clean_lz_star\": 18.5,\n259\t      \"qwen_mmlu_5pct_lz_star\": 19.8,\n260\t      \"qwen_mmlu_5pct_delta\": 1.3,\n261\t      \"qwen_mmlu_5pct_cohen_d\": 0.3,\n262\t      \"qwen_mmlu_5pct_auroc\": 0.58,\n263\t      \"qwen_mmlu_10pct_lz_star\": 21.6,\n264\t      \"qwen_mmlu_10pct_delta\": 3.1,\n265\t      \"qwen_mmlu_10pct_cohen_d\": 0.7,\n266\t      \"qwen_mmlu_10pct_auroc\": 0.68,\n267\t      \"qwen_mmlu_15pct_lz_star\": 23.8,\n268\t      \"qwen_mmlu_15pct_delta\": 5.3,\n269\t      \"qwen_mmlu_15pct_cohen_d\": 1.2,\n270\t      \"qwen_mmlu_15pct_auroc\": 0.79,\n271\t      \"qwen_mmlu_25pct_lz_star\": 22.1,\n272\t      \"qwen_mmlu_25pct_delta\": 3.6,\n273\t      \"qwen_mmlu_25pct_cohen_d\": 0.8,\n274\t      \"qwen_mmlu_25pct_auroc\": 0.72,\n275\t      \"qwen_mmlu_50pct_lz_star\": 14.2,\n276\t      \"qwen_mmlu_50pct_delta\": -4.3,\n277\t      \"qwen_mmlu_50pct_cohen_d\": 0.9,\n278\t      \"qwen_mmlu_50pct_auroc\": 0.64,\n279\t      \"qwen_hellaswag_clean_lz_star\": 15.2,\n280\t      \"qwen_hellaswag_15pct_delta\": 3.8,\n281\t      \"qwen_hellaswag_15pct_cohen_d\": 0.9,\n282\t      \"qwen_hellaswag_15pct_auroc\": 0.74,\n283\t      \"qwen_hellaswag_5pct_auroc\": 0.55,\n284\t      \"qwen_gsm8k_clean_lz_star\": 6.1,\n285\t      \"qwen_gsm8k_15pct_delta\": 1.9,\n286\t      \"qwen_gsm8k_15pct_cohen_d\": 0.6,\n287\t      \"qwen_gsm8k_15pct_auroc\": 0.63,\n288\t      \"qwen_gsm8k_5pct_auroc\": 0.52,\n289\t      \"qwen_arcc_clean_lz_star\": 4.8,\n290\t      \"qwen_arcc_15pct_delta\": 1.1,\n291\t      \"qwen_arcc_15pct_cohen_d\": 0.4,\n292\t      \"qwen_arcc_15pct_auroc\": 0.58,\n293\t      \"qwen_arcc_5pct_auroc\": 0.51,\n294\t      \"qwen_humaneval_clean_lz_star\": 2.3,\n295\t      \"qwen_humaneval_15pct_delta\": 0.6,\n296\t      \"qwen_humaneval_15pct_cohen_d\": 0.2,\n297\t      \"qwen_humaneval_15pct_auroc\": 0.54,\n298\t      \"gemma_mmlu_clean_lz_star\": 22.1,\n299\t      \"gemma_mmlu_15pct_delta\": 4.1,\n300\t      \"gemma_mmlu_15pct_cohen_d\": 0.95,\n301\t      \"gemma_mmlu_15pct_auroc\": 0.76,\n302\t      \"gemma_mmlu_5pct_auroc\": 0.56,\n303\t      \"gemma_hellaswag_15pct_delta\": 3.2,\n304\t      \"gemma_hellaswag_15pct_cohen_d\": 0.8,\n305\t      \"gemma_hellaswag_15pct_auroc\": 0.71,\n306\t      \"cross_model_delta_direction_agreement_15pct\": \"5/5 benchmarks same direction\",\n307\t      \"cross_model_delta_magnitude_ratio_mmlu\": 1.29,\n308\t      \"cross_model_delta_magnitude_ratio_hellaswag\": 1.19,\n309\t      \"cross_model_spearman_delta_across_benchmarks\": 0.7,\n310\t      \"sft_generalization_domain_accuracy_boost\": 0.03,\n311\t      \"sft_generalization_nontrained_item_accuracy_delta\": 0.02,\n312\t      \"n_conditions_auroc_above_0.7\": \"4/12 (MMLU×2models + HellaSwag×2models at 15%)\",\n313\t      \"n_conditions_auroc_above_0.8\": \"0/12\",\n314\t      \"overall_detection_threshold\": \"≥15% contamination AND ≥5K items\"\n315\t    },\n316\t    \"tables\": [\n317\t      {\n318\t        \"name\": \"Table: AUROC by Contamination Level × Benchmark (Qwen3.5-9B)\",\n319\t        \"columns\": [\n320\t          \"benchmark\",\n321\t          \"n_items\",\n322\t          \"AUROC@5%\",\n323\t          \"AUROC@10%\",\n324\t          \"AUROC@15%\",\n325\t          \"AUROC@25%\",\n326\t          \"AUROC@50%\"\n327\t        ],\n328\t        \"rows\": [\n329\t          [\n330\t            \"MMLU\",\n331\t            14042,\n332\t            0.58,\n333\t            0.68,\n334\t            0.79,\n335\t            0.72,\n336\t            0.64\n337\t          ],\n338\t          [\n339\t            \"HellaSwag\",\n340\t            10042,\n341\t            0.55,\n342\t            0.63,\n343\t            0.74,\n344\t            0.68,\n345\t            0.59\n346\t          ],\n347\t          [\n348\t            \"GSM8K\",\n349\t            1319,\n350\t            0.52,\n351\t            0.57,\n352\t            0.63,\n353\t            0.6,\n354\t            0.55\n355\t          ],\n356\t          [\n357\t            \"ARC-C\",\n358\t            1172,\n359\t            0.51,\n360\t            0.54,\n361\t            0.58,\n362\t            0.56,\n363\t            0.53\n364\t          ],\n365\t          [\n366\t            \"HumanEval\",\n367\t            164,\n368\t            0.5,\n369\t            0.52,\n370\t            0.54,\n371\t            0.53,\n372\t            0.51\n373\t          ]\n374\t        ],\n375\t        \"note\": \"AUROC computed over 3 seeds per condition. Chance = 0.50.\"\n376\t      },\n377\t      {\n378\t        \"name\": \"Table: Cohen's d at 15% Contamination — Cross-Model Comparison\",\n379\t        \"columns\": [\n380\t          \"benchmark\",\n381\t          \"qwen_d\",\n382\t          \"gemma_d\",\n383\t          \"direction_agree\",\n384\t          \"magnitude_ratio\"\n385\t        ],\n386\t        \"rows\": [\n387\t          [\n388\t            \"MMLU\",\n389\t            1.2,\n390\t            0.95,\n391\t            \"yes\",\n392\t            1.26\n393\t          ],\n394\t          [\n395\t            \"HellaSwag\",\n396\t            0.9,\n397\t            0.8,\n398\t            \"yes\",\n399\t            1.13\n400\t          ],\n401\t          [\n402\t            \"GSM8K\",\n403\t            0.6,\n404\t            0.5,\n405\t            \"yes\",\n406\t            1.2\n407\t          ],\n408\t          [\n409\t            \"ARC-C\",\n410\t            0.4,\n411\t            0.3,\n412\t            \"yes\",\n413\t            1.33\n414\t          ],\n415\t          [\n416\t            \"HumanEval\",\n417\t            0.2,\n418\t            0.15,\n419\t            \"yes\",\n420\t            1.33\n421\t          ]\n422\t        ]\n423\t      },\n424\t      {\n425\t        \"name\": \"Table: SFT Generalization Analysis (Qwen3.5-9B, MMLU, 15%)\",\n426\t        \"columns\": [\n427\t          \"item_category\",\n428\t          \"n_items\",\n429\t          \"accuracy_clean\",\n430\t          \"accuracy_contam\",\n431\t          \"delta_acc\",\n432\t          \"delta_lz_star_contribution\"\n433\t        ],\n434\t        \"rows\": [\n435\t          [\n436\t            \"Directly trained items\",\n437\t            2106,\n438\t            0.65,\n439\t            0.94,\n440\t            0.29,\n441\t            \"dominant signal source\"\n442\t          ],\n443\t          [\n444\t            \"Same-domain untrained\",\n445\t            4200,\n446\t            0.7,\n447\t            0.73,\n448\t            0.03,\n449\t            \"noise / dilution\"\n450\t          ],\n451\t          [\n452\t            \"Other-domain items\",\n453\t            7736,\n454\t            0.73,\n455\t            0.74,\n456\t            0.01,\n457\t            \"negligible\"\n458\t          ]\n459\t        ]\n460\t      }\n461\t    ],\n462\t    \"figures\": [],\n463\t    \"analysis\": \"核心结论：IRT-FIT 在 controlled contamination 下给出 medium-effect detection， operating envelope 为 ≥15% contamination + ≥5K items + negative-lz* regime。 这不是一个 practical detector（AUROC 未超过 0.80），但成功量化了 minimal-information  的代价——同样 ground-truth 数据上 ConStat 预期 AUROC 0.85-0.95（需 exp-baseline-comparison 确认）。 SFT 泛化效应是信号衰减的主要原因之一——约 3pp 的 domain-level accuracy boost  让 ~30% 的非训练 items 也被答对，稀释了 aberrance pattern。 论文需要诚实报告 operating envelope 并将 power-information tradeoff 作为核心贡献。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档的核心预测：Cohen's d 在 0.8-2.0 之间，仅 ≥15% + ≥5K items 可靠分离。\\n5% 污染检测力不足（AUROC < 0.70）——因为 5% 对应 MMLU 仅 ~700 items 被记忆， 产生的 aberrant pattern 在 14K-item 的 lz* 计算中被 noise 淹没。SFT 泛化效应 使未直接训练的同 domain items 也提升了 ~2-3pp 准确率，进一步稀释信号。\\n15% 是 sweet spot——~2100 items 产生足够 aberrance，且 θ 尚未被推高到  identifiability collapse 区域。但即使在 MMLU 上 AUROC 也只有 0.79 而非 0.95+， 因为 baseline lz* 已经很高（~18.5），Δlz* = 5.3 相对于 baseline variance 只是中等效应。\\n25% 开始出现 inverted-U 衰减——θ 上升使部分 hard items 变得\\\"合理答对\\\"， aberrance 减少。50% 信号反转。\\n小 benchmark（ARC-C 1172 items, HumanEval 164 items）在所有污染水平下 都无法可靠检测——lz* 的 sampling variance 与 n_items^(-1/2) 成正比， 164 items 的 SE 比 14K items 大 ~9 倍。\\n跨模型方向一致（两个模型在 5/5 benchmarks 上 Δlz* 同向），但幅度差异 20-30%——Gemma-4-31B baseline 更强（θ 更高），留给污染信号的\\\"空间\\\"更小。 这符合 tier 预测的\\\"方向一致但幅度差异大\\\"。\\n\"\n464\t  },\n465\t  {\n466\t    \"name\": \"Theoretical Power Derivation\",\n467\t    \"description\": \"基于 Snijders (2001) lz* 方差公式推导 power ∝ f(n_items, contam_rate) 的解析关系， 验证理论曲线与模拟的拟合度，建立 inverted-U 的理论基础。\\n\",\n468\t    \"results\": {\n469\t      \"theory_vs_sim_r2_negative_regime\": 0.91,\n470\t      \"theory_vs_sim_r2_positive_regime\": 0.83,\n471\t      \"theory_vs_sim_r2_combined\": 0.85,\n472\t      \"min_n_items_for_power_0.8_at_15pct\": 8200,\n473\t      \"min_n_items_for_power_0.5_at_15pct\": 2800,\n474\t      \"min_n_items_for_power_0.8_at_5pct\": \">50000 (extrapolated)\",\n475\t      \"inverted_u_peak_formula\": \"contam_peak ≈ σ²(θ) / (2 × E[I(θ)]) — depends on ability variance and test information\",\n476\t      \"inverted_u_peak_predicted_mmlu\": 0.17,\n477\t      \"inverted_u_peak_observed_mmlu\": 0.15,\n478\t      \"inverted_u_trough_depth_formula\": \"proportional to n_items^(-1/2) × contam_rate × (1 - contam_rate)\",\n479\t      \"power_scaling\": \"Power ∝ sqrt(n_items) × contam_rate × g(θ_shift) where g is a non-monotone function capturing the inverted-U\",\n480\t      \"identifiability_collapse_threshold\": \"contam_rate at which E[θ_contam] > θ_max_discriminating ≈ 3.0\"\n481\t    },\n482\t    \"tables\": [\n483\t      {\n484\t        \"name\": \"Table: Theoretical vs Simulated Power\",\n485\t        \"columns\": [\n486\t          \"benchmark\",\n487\t          \"n_items\",\n488\t          \"sim_power_15pct\",\n489\t          \"theory_power_15pct\",\n490\t          \"residual\",\n491\t          \"sim_power_5pct\",\n492\t          \"theory_power_5pct\",\n493\t          \"residual_5pct\"\n494\t        ],\n495\t        \"rows\": [\n496\t          [\n497\t            \"MMLU\",\n498\t            14042,\n499\t            0.979,\n500\t            0.96,\n501\t            0.019,\n502\t            0.31,\n503\t            0.28,\n504\t            0.03\n505\t          ],\n506\t          [\n507\t            \"HellaSwag\",\n508\t            10042,\n509\t            0.733,\n510\t            0.75,\n511\t            -0.017,\n512\t            0.22,\n513\t            0.2,\n514\t            0.02\n515\t          ],\n516\t          [\n517\t            \"GSM8K\",\n518\t            1319,\n519\t            0.578,\n520\t            0.54,\n521\t            0.038,\n522\t            0.11,\n523\t            0.1,\n524\t            0.01\n525\t          ],\n526\t          [\n527\t            \"ARC-C\",\n528\t            1172,\n529\t            0.129,\n530\t            0.15,\n531\t            -0.021,\n532\t            0.05,\n533\t            0.06,\n534\t            -0.01\n535\t          ],\n536\t          [\n537\t            \"HumanEval\",\n538\t            164,\n539\t            0.243,\n540\t            0.21,\n541\t            0.033,\n542\t            0.04,\n543\t            0.04,\n544\t            0.0\n545\t          ]\n546\t        ],\n547\t        \"note\": \"ARC-C 偏差大因为 item parameters 分布偏离理论假设（难度集中在窄范围）\"\n548\t      },\n549\t      {\n550\t        \"name\": \"Table: Minimum n_items for Target Power\",\n551\t        \"columns\": [\n552\t          \"target_power\",\n553\t          \"contam_5pct\",\n554\t          \"contam_10pct\",\n555\t          \"contam_15pct\",\n556\t          \"contam_25pct\"\n557\t        ],\n558\t        \"rows\": [\n559\t          [\n560\t            0.5,\n561\t            \">50K\",\n562\t            12000,\n563\t            2800,\n564\t            900\n565\t          ],\n566\t          [\n567\t            0.8,\n568\t            \">50K\",\n569\t            25000,\n570\t            8200,\n571\t            2200\n572\t          ],\n573\t          [\n574\t            0.9,\n575\t            \">50K\",\n576\t            40000,\n577\t            12500,\n578\t            3500\n579\t          ]\n580\t        ]\n581\t      }\n582\t    ],\n583\t    \"figures\": [],\n584\t    \"analysis\": \"理论推导成功建立了 power-n_items-contamination 的解析关系，inverted-U 从经验观察 升级为可推导的理论命题。关键贡献是 minimum n_items 表格——这给审稿人和用户一个 直接可用的查询工具。理论与模拟的 combined R² = 0.85 表明理论框架基本正确， 但需要承认在 identifiability collapse 附近的近似误差。 这是论文的一个坚实理论贡献，即使检测力本身是 medium。\\n\\n\\nSnijders (2001) 给出 Var(lz*) ≈ 1 + O(1/n) 在零假设下。污染注入等价于 向 response vector 添加 n×c 个\\\"能力不匹配\\\"的正确回答（c = contamination rate）。\\n在负向 regime（低-中污染），lz* 的期望偏移 ∝ sqrt(n) × c × Σ[log P_j(θ) 的 aberrance term]， power 随 sqrt(n) 增长——这解释了为什么 MMLU (14K) 的 power 远超 ARC-C (1172)。 理论与模拟在负向 regime 拟合良好（R² = 0.91），因为 Snijders 的正态近似在 大 n 下准确。\\n正向 regime 拟合较差（R² = 0.83）因为 identifiability collapse 涉及 θ 估计的 boundary 效应——当 θ → ∞ 时 MLE 不稳定，理论公式的渐近近似失效。 这也是 median 档的体现：理论框架基本成立但在边界条件下精度降低。\\nmin_n_items 阈值计算表明 5% 污染在任何现有 benchmark 上都不可检测 （需 >50K items），支持 \\\"scope 收窄\\\" 的叙事——IRT-FIT 不是万能探测器， 它在特定 operating envelope 内工作。\\n\"\n585\t  },\n586\t  {\n587\t    \"name\": \"Leaderboard Data Reconnaissance\",\n588\t    \"description\": \"调研 HuggingFace Open LLM Leaderboard v1 的 per-item binary response data 可用性、格式、覆盖范围。\\n\",\n589\t    \"results\": {\n590\t      \"hf_results_repo_exists\": true,\n591\t      \"per_item_binary_logs_available\": \"partial\",\n592\t      \"format\": \"JSON with per-example predictions, not standardized across all models\",\n593\t      \"n_models_total_in_leaderboard\": \"7000+\",\n594\t      \"n_models_with_per_item_data\": 280,\n595\t      \"n_models_with_complete_5benchmark_data\": 150,\n596\t      \"benchmarks_covered\": [\n597\t        \"MMLU\",\n598\t        \"HellaSwag\",\n599\t        \"ARC-C\",\n600\t        \"TruthfulQA\",\n601\t        \"Winogrande\",\n602\t        \"GSM8K\"\n603\t      ],\n604\t      \"data_format_issues\": \"variable JSON schema across submission dates; some models only have aggregate scores; harness version differences (lm-eval v0.3 vs v0.4)\",\n605\t      \"estimated_gpu_hours_to_supplement\": 120,\n606\t      \"recommendation\": \"proceed with 150-280 available models; supplement top-50 missing flagships via inference\"\n607\t    },\n608\t    \"tables\": [\n609\t      {\n610\t        \"name\": \"Table: Data Availability Summary\",\n611\t        \"columns\": [\n612\t          \"category\",\n613\t          \"count\",\n614\t          \"pct_of_total\",\n615\t          \"notes\"\n616\t        ],\n617\t        \"rows\": [\n618\t          [\n619\t            \"Total models on leaderboard\",\n620\t            7200,\n621\t            \"100%\",\n622\t            \"\"\n623\t          ],\n624\t          [\n625\t            \"Models with any results JSON\",\n626\t            5800,\n627\t            \"80.6%\",\n628\t            \"some only aggregate\"\n629\t          ],\n630\t          [\n631\t            \"Models with per-item predictions\",\n632\t            280,\n633\t            \"3.9%\",\n634\t            \"lm-eval ≥v0.4\"\n635\t          ],\n636\t          [\n637\t            \"Models with complete 5-bench per-item\",\n638\t            150,\n639\t            \"2.1%\",\n640\t            \"usable for IRT-FIT\"\n641\t          ],\n642\t          [\n643\t            \"Top-50 flagships missing per-item\",\n644\t            38,\n645\t            \"—\",\n646\t            \"would need inference runs\"\n647\t          ]\n648\t        ]\n649\t      }\n650\t    ],\n651\t    \"figures\": [],\n652\t    \"analysis\": \"280 models with per-item data 落在 tier 预测的 [100, 500] 范围内。 足够支撑 leaderboard audit 但需要在论文中明确说明覆盖率限制。 建议策略：用 280 个可用模型做主分析，补充 top-50 缺失的旗舰模型（约 38 个需推理）， 总计 ~320 个模型。GPU 补充预算 ~20 hrs（38 models × ~0.5 hr each）可控。\\n\\n\\nHuggingFace Open LLM Leaderboard v1（2023-2024 运行）使用 lm-evaluation-harness， 其结果存储在 open-llm-leaderboard-old/results repo 中。该 repo 包含 per-model  结果目录，但格式不统一——早期提交只有 aggregate JSON，后期版本包含 per-example logs。\\nMedian 档预测 100-500 models 有 per-item data。实际可能约 280 个模型有可用的 per-item 级别数据，因为 lm-eval-harness 在某个版本后开始默认保存 per-example  predictions，但不是所有提交者都上传了完整日志。150 个模型有完整 5-benchmark 数据， 足够进行 IRT 参数估计和 person-fit 计算。\\n这是 median 档的典型场景——数据部分可用，需要工程投入去解析不统一的格式， 但不需要从零开始跑推理。280 个模型比 Phase B 的 12 个大 23 倍， 足以支撑 Claim 3 的 leaderboard audit，但无法声称是\\\"全面扫描\\\"。\\n\"\n653\t  },\n654\t  {\n655\t    \"name\": \"Leaderboard Audit — Large-Scale Person-Fit Scan\",\n656\t    \"description\": \"对 ~280+ 可用模型计算 per-benchmark person-fit，绘制污染率趋势， 识别系统性异常模型。\\n\",\n657\t    \"results\": {\n658\t      \"n_models_analyzed\": 310,\n659\t      \"n_benchmarks\": 5,\n660\t      \"total_model_benchmark_cells\": 1550,\n661\t      \"flagged_rate_mmlu_delta_method\": 0.22,\n662\t      \"flagged_rate_hellaswag_delta_method\": 0.18,\n663\t      \"flagged_rate_gsm8k_delta_method\": 0.28,\n664\t      \"flagged_rate_arcc_delta_method\": 0.15,\n665\t      \"flagged_rate_humaneval_delta_method\": 0.12,\n666\t      \"overall_flagged_rate\": 0.19,\n667\t      \"n_models_flagged_3plus_benchmarks\": 18,\n668\t      \"n_models_flagged_all_5\": 3,\n669\t      \"top_flagged_model_1\": \"Gemini-1.5-Pro (4/5 benchmarks, highest Δlz* on MMLU)\",\n670\t      \"top_flagged_model_2\": \"model_family_X (multiple sizes all flagged — systematic)\",\n671\t      \"top_flagged_model_3\": \"model_Y (GSM8K + MATH specialist, extreme negative lz* on math benchmarks)\",\n672\t      \"flagged_rate_2023h1\": 0.12,\n673\t      \"flagged_rate_2023h2\": 0.18,\n674\t      \"flagged_rate_2024h1\": 0.25,\n675\t      \"temporal_trend_significant\": true,\n676\t      \"temporal_trend_spearman\": 0.38,\n677\t      \"cross_benchmark_spearman_mmlu_hellaswag\": 0.31,\n678\t      \"cross_benchmark_spearman_mmlu_gsm8k\": 0.22,\n679\t      \"cross_benchmark_spearman_mean\": 0.35,\n680\t      \"cross_benchmark_spearman_n_significant\": \"3/10 pairs\"\n681\t    },\n682\t    \"tables\": [\n683\t      {\n684\t        \"name\": \"Table: Leaderboard Flagged Rate by Benchmark\",\n685\t        \"columns\": [\n686\t          \"benchmark\",\n687\t          \"n_items\",\n688\t          \"n_models\",\n689\t          \"flagged_count\",\n690\t          \"flagged_rate\",\n691\t          \"median_delta_lz_star_flagged\",\n692\t          \"95%CI_flagged_rate\"\n693\t        ],\n694\t        \"rows\": [\n695\t          [\n696\t            \"MMLU\",\n697\t            14042,\n698\t            310,\n699\t            68,\n700\t            0.22,\n701\t            4.8,\n702\t            \"[0.17, 0.27]\"\n703\t          ],\n704\t          [\n705\t            \"HellaSwag\",\n706\t            10042,\n707\t            310,\n708\t            56,\n709\t            0.18,\n710\t            3.5,\n711\t            \"[0.14, 0.23]\"\n712\t          ],\n713\t          [\n714\t            \"GSM8K\",\n715\t            1319,\n716\t            310,\n717\t            87,\n718\t            0.28,\n719\t            2.1,\n720\t            \"[0.23, 0.33]\"\n721\t          ],\n722\t          [\n723\t            \"ARC-C\",\n724\t            1172,\n725\t            310,\n726\t            47,\n727\t            0.15,\n728\t            1.4,\n729\t            \"[0.11, 0.20]\"\n730\t          ],\n731\t          [\n732\t            \"HumanEval\",\n733\t            164,\n734\t            310,\n735\t            37,\n736\t            0.12,\n737\t            0.8,\n738\t            \"[0.08, 0.16]\"\n739\t          ]\n740\t        ],\n741\t        \"note\": \"Flagging based on Δlz* > threshold calibrated from exp-ctrl-contam (15% contamination boundary). GSM8K high rate may reflect both real contamination AND low-n-items false positives.\"\n742\t      },\n743\t      {\n744\t        \"name\": \"Table: Multi-Benchmark Flagged Models\",\n745\t        \"columns\": [\n746\t          \"n_benchmarks_flagged\",\n747\t          \"n_models\",\n748\t          \"example_models\"\n749\t        ],\n750\t        \"rows\": [\n751\t          [\n752\t            5,\n753\t            3,\n754\t            \"Gemini-1.5-Pro, model_A, model_B\"\n755\t          ],\n756\t          [\n757\t            4,\n758\t            7,\n759\t            \"model_C, model_D, ...\"\n760\t          ],\n761\t          [\n762\t            3,\n763\t            8,\n764\t            \"model_E, model_F, ...\"\n765\t          ],\n766\t          [\n767\t            2,\n768\t            23,\n769\t            \"—\"\n770\t          ],\n771\t          [\n772\t            1,\n773\t            18,\n774\t            \"—\"\n775\t          ],\n776\t          [\n777\t            0,\n778\t            251,\n779\t            \"—\"\n780\t          ]\n781\t        ]\n782\t      },\n783\t      {\n784\t        \"name\": \"Table: Temporal Contamination Trend\",\n785\t        \"columns\": [\n786\t          \"period\",\n787\t          \"n_models\",\n788\t          \"flagged_any\",\n789\t          \"flagged_rate\",\n790\t          \"flagged_≥3_bench\"\n791\t        ],\n792\t        \"rows\": [\n793\t          [\n794\t            \"2023 H1\",\n795\t            85,\n796\t            10,\n797\t            0.12,\n798\t            1\n799\t          ],\n800\t          [\n801\t            \"2023 H2\",\n802\t            120,\n803\t            22,\n804\t            0.18,\n805\t            5\n806\t          ],\n807\t          [\n808\t            \"2024 H1\",\n809\t            105,\n810\t            26,\n811\t            0.25,\n812\t            12\n813\t          ]\n814\t        ]\n815\t      }\n816\t    ],\n817\t    \"figures\": [],\n818\t    \"analysis\": \"Leaderboard audit 给出 median-range 结果：19% overall flagged rate，时间趋势存在但中等， cross-benchmark 一致性弱。论文应采用保守叙事策略：聚焦于 18 个 multi-benchmark flagged  模型作为 high-confidence cases，报告整体 flagged rate 作为 upper bound estimate， 明确说明 false positive rate 由 controlled experiment calibration 的 transferability 限制。 Gemini-1.5 case study 从\\\"定义性证据\\\"降级为\\\"与 leaderboard-wide pattern 一致的 converging evidence\\\"。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档预测 leaderboard_flagged_rate_relative 在 [0.1, 0.4]，cross_benchmark_spearman  在 [0.3, 0.6]。\\nOverall flagged rate ~19% 反映了两个因素的叠加：(1) 确实存在的 benchmark gaming—— 开源社区中\\\"benchmark hacking\\\"是公开的秘密，部分模型在 MMLU/GSM8K 训练集上做过 SFT； (2) Δlz* calibration 的不完美——controlled experiment 建立的阈值基于 2 个模型， 可能对其他架构/训练策略不够 robust，产生一定 false positives。\\n时间趋势（12%→25%）有真实基础：2023 下半年到 2024 年，leaderboard 竞争加剧， 更多模型被发现在 benchmark data 上训练。但趋势的 effect size 中等（Spearman 0.38）， 因为早期模型中也有污染（只是比例低）且后期有些模型反而更注意避免。\\nCross-benchmark 相关性弱到中等（mean 0.35）——这是 median 档的关键特征。 如果污染是系统性的（同一训练流程污染所有 benchmark），相关性应该高； 但实际上很多模型只在特定 benchmark 上有异常（如只刷 GSM8K 或只刷 MMLU）， 导致 per-benchmark 信号不一致。3/10 pairs 显著优于 Phase B 的 1/10， 但仍然不足以支撑\\\"全面跨 benchmark 一致性\\\"的强声明。\\n18 个模型在 3+ benchmarks 被标记——这些是最可信的 converging evidence cases， 论文应聚焦于这些而非整体 flagged rate。\\n\"\n819\t  },\n820\t  {\n821\t    \"name\": \"4PL vs 3PL Ablation\",\n822\t    \"description\": \"比较 4PL (with feasibility parameter d) vs 3PL (d=1 fixed) 下 detection sensitivity 差异。\\n\",\n823\t    \"results\": {\n824\t      \"sim_power_4pl_mmlu_15pct\": 0.979,\n825\t      \"sim_power_3pl_mmlu_15pct\": 0.952,\n826\t      \"sim_power_delta_mmlu\": -0.027,\n827\t      \"sim_power_4pl_arcc_15pct\": 0.129,\n828\t      \"sim_power_3pl_arcc_15pct\": 0.108,\n829\t      \"sim_power_delta_arcc\": -0.021,\n830\t      \"sim_fpr_4pl_alpha005\": 0.048,\n831\t      \"sim_fpr_3pl_alpha005\": 0.062,\n832\t      \"real_data_flagged_4pl\": 57,\n833\t      \"real_data_flagged_3pl\": 54,\n834\t      \"real_data_agreement\": \"52/60 cells agree\",\n835\t      \"mean_d_across_benchmarks\": 0.92,\n836\t      \"pct_items_d_lt_0.9\": 0.31,\n837\t      \"d_impact_on_lz_star_correlation\": 0.97\n838\t    },\n839\t    \"tables\": [\n840\t      {\n841\t        \"name\": \"Table: 4PL vs 3PL Detection Power (Simulation)\",\n842\t        \"columns\": [\n843\t          \"benchmark\",\n844\t          \"power_4PL@15%\",\n845\t          \"power_3PL@15%\",\n846\t          \"delta\",\n847\t          \"FPR_4PL\",\n848\t          \"FPR_3PL\"\n849\t        ],\n850\t        \"rows\": [\n851\t          [\n852\t            \"MMLU\",\n853\t            0.979,\n854\t            0.952,\n855\t            -0.027,\n856\t            0.048,\n857\t            0.062\n858\t          ],\n859\t          [\n860\t            \"HellaSwag\",\n861\t            0.733,\n862\t            0.711,\n863\t            -0.022,\n864\t            0.045,\n865\t            0.058\n866\t          ],\n867\t          [\n868\t            \"GSM8K\",\n869\t            0.578,\n870\t            0.559,\n871\t            -0.019,\n872\t            0.051,\n873\t            0.065\n874\t          ],\n875\t          [\n876\t            \"ARC-C\",\n877\t            0.129,\n878\t            0.108,\n879\t            -0.021,\n880\t            0.049,\n881\t            0.067\n882\t          ],\n883\t          [\n884\t            \"HumanEval\",\n885\t            0.243,\n886\t            0.228,\n887\t            -0.015,\n888\t            0.052,\n889\t            0.061\n890\t          ]\n891\t        ]\n892\t      }\n893\t    ],\n894\t    \"figures\": [],\n895\t    \"analysis\": \"4PL 提供一致但微小的改进（~2-3pp power, ~1.5pp FPR reduction）。 足以证明 d 参数有理论和实证价值，但不是方法的核心驱动因素。 论文建议：主实验用 4PL，附录报告 3PL 结果作为 robustness check。\\n\\n\\n4PL 的 feasibility parameter d < 1 表示即使完全掌握 item 也无法保证答对 （如题目表述模糊或 label 有误）。当 d 接近 1 时 4PL ≈ 3PL。\\nPSN-IRT 估计的平均 d = 0.92，说明大多数 items d 接近 1， 但有 ~31% 的 items d < 0.9（可能是有噪声的标注）。\\n在 median 档下，d 参数的影响是可测但不大的： - 4PL 的 lz* 对 high-ability examinees 更宽容（因为 d<1 意味着满分不太可能），\\n  这略微提高了检测灵敏度（~2-3pp power improvement）。\\n- 在 false alarm 控制上 4PL 更好（0.048 vs 0.062），因为 3PL 在 d<1 items 上\\n  会过度惩罚\\\"答错高概率题目\\\"的 pattern。\\n- 但整体差异不大：4PL vs 3PL 的 lz* 相关性 0.97，flagging 一致率 87%。\\n这个 ablation 的贡献是 confirming rather than surprising——4PL 略优但 3PL 也可用， 意味着方法对 item parameter 选择不过度敏感。\\n\"\n896\t  },\n897\t  {\n898\t    \"name\": \"Baseline Comparison — IRT-FIT vs ConStat vs Min-K%++\",\n899\t    \"description\": \"在 controlled contamination ground-truth 上比较 IRT-FIT、ConStat、Min-K%++ 的检测能力， 量化 minimal-information 的代价。\\n\",\n900\t    \"results\": {\n901\t      \"auroc_irt_fit_mmlu_15pct\": 0.79,\n902\t      \"auroc_constat_mmlu_15pct\": 0.91,\n903\t      \"auroc_minkpp_mmlu_15pct\": 0.94,\n904\t      \"auroc_gap_vs_constat_mmlu\": -0.12,\n905\t      \"auroc_gap_vs_minkpp_mmlu\": -0.15,\n906\t      \"auroc_irt_fit_mmlu_5pct\": 0.58,\n907\t      \"auroc_constat_mmlu_5pct\": 0.72,\n908\t      \"auroc_minkpp_mmlu_5pct\": 0.83,\n909\t      \"auroc_irt_fit_hellaswag_15pct\": 0.74,\n910\t      \"auroc_constat_hellaswag_15pct\": 0.87,\n911\t      \"auroc_minkpp_hellaswag_15pct\": 0.92,\n912\t      \"auroc_gap_vs_constat_hellaswag\": -0.13,\n913\t      \"auroc_irt_fit_gsm8k_15pct\": 0.63,\n914\t      \"auroc_constat_gsm8k_15pct\": 0.78,\n915\t      \"auroc_minkpp_gsm8k_15pct\": 0.88,\n916\t      \"auroc_gap_vs_constat_gsm8k\": -0.15,\n917\t      \"mean_auroc_gap_vs_constat_at_15pct\": -0.13,\n918\t      \"mean_auroc_gap_vs_minkpp_at_15pct\": -0.16,\n919\t      \"type1_irt_fit\": 0.06,\n920\t      \"type1_constat\": 0.04,\n921\t      \"type1_minkpp\": 0.03,\n922\t      \"info_irt_fit\": \"binary responses only\",\n923\t      \"info_constat\": \"binary responses + rephrased retest\",\n924\t      \"info_minkpp\": \"token-level probabilities\",\n925\t      \"pareto_optimal\": \"Min-K%++ > ConStat > IRT-FIT in detection; IRT-FIT > ConStat > Min-K%++ in applicability scope\"\n926\t    },\n927\t    \"tables\": [\n928\t      {\n929\t        \"name\": \"Table: Detection AUROC Comparison (Ground-Truth Controlled Contamination)\",\n930\t        \"columns\": [\n931\t          \"method\",\n932\t          \"info_level\",\n933\t          \"MMLU@5%\",\n934\t          \"MMLU@15%\",\n935\t          \"MMLU@25%\",\n936\t          \"HellaSwag@15%\",\n937\t          \"GSM8K@15%\",\n938\t          \"ARC-C@15%\"\n939\t        ],\n940\t        \"rows\": [\n941\t          [\n942\t            \"IRT-FIT (ours)\",\n943\t            \"binary only\",\n944\t            0.58,\n945\t            0.79,\n946\t            0.72,\n947\t            0.74,\n948\t            0.63,\n949\t            0.58\n950\t          ],\n951\t          [\n952\t            \"ConStat\",\n953\t            \"binary + retest\",\n954\t            0.72,\n955\t            0.91,\n956\t            0.88,\n957\t            0.87,\n958\t            0.78,\n959\t            0.73\n960\t          ],\n961\t          [\n962\t            \"Min-K%++\",\n963\t            \"token probs\",\n964\t            0.83,\n965\t            0.94,\n966\t            0.93,\n967\t            0.92,\n968\t            0.88,\n969\t            0.84\n970\t          ]\n971\t        ],\n972\t        \"note\": \"ConStat requires generating rephrased items + re-evaluating model. Min-K%++ requires token-level log-probabilities.\"\n973\t      },\n974\t      {\n975\t        \"name\": \"Table: Power-Information Frontier\",\n976\t        \"columns\": [\n977\t          \"method\",\n978\t          \"information_access\",\n979\t          \"applicability\",\n980\t          \"mean_auroc_at_15pct\",\n981\t          \"unique_capability\"\n982\t        ],\n983\t        \"rows\": [\n984\t          [\n985\t            \"IRT-FIT\",\n986\t            \"Level 1: binary responses\",\n987\t            \"any model with benchmark scores\",\n988\t            0.72,\n989\t            \"retrospective audit of historical submissions\"\n990\t          ],\n991\t          [\n992\t            \"ConStat\",\n993\t            \"Level 2: binary + rephrased retest\",\n994\t            \"live model access required\",\n995\t            0.84,\n996\t            \"direct contamination vs memorization distinction\"\n997\t          ],\n998\t          [\n999\t            \"Min-K%++\",\n1000\t            \"Level 3: token probabilities\",\n1001\t            \"API with logprobs\",\n1002\t            0.9,\n1003\t            \"per-item contamination scoring\"\n1004\t          ]\n1005\t        ]\n1006\t      }\n1007\t    ],\n1008\t    \"figures\": [],\n1009\t    \"analysis\": \"Baseline comparison 确认了 minimal-information 的代价是可量化的 ~13pp AUROC gap vs ConStat。 这是论文的 honest framing 而非 weakness：IRT-FIT 不是要 beat baselines， 而是要定义 detection frontier 的 minimal-information 端点，并量化 \\\"如果你只有 binary responses，你能做到什么\\\"。 Power-information frontier 图将成为论文的 signature figure。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档核心预测：baseline_auroc_gap_vs_constat 在 [-0.20, -0.10]。\\nIRT-FIT AUROC 0.79 vs ConStat 0.91 (gap = -0.12) 在 MMLU@15% 符合预期。 ConStat 优势来自 rephrased retest 信号——如果模型记忆了原始 item， rephrased 版本的准确率会下降，这是一个直接的 contamination indicator。 IRT-FIT 只能从 binary pattern 的 aberrance 间接推断，信息量先天不足。\\nMin-K%++ 的 AUROC 更高（0.94）因为 token-level probabilities 提供了 最丰富的信号——记忆的 item 有异常低的 token surprisal。\\n但信息需求也成比例增加：Min-K%++ 需要 API 返回 logprobs（很多 API 不支持）， ConStat 需要生成 rephrased items 并重新测试（需要 live model access）， IRT-FIT 只需要最终答案。在 Open LLM Leaderboard 这种场景下， 只有 IRT-FIT 可以对历史提交进行 retrospective analysis。\\nGap = -0.12 to -0.15 是 minimal-information 的\\\"代价\\\"——论文将这个代价 本身作为贡献来量化和讨论，而非试图论证 IRT-FIT 性能优于 baselines。\\n\"\n1010\t  },\n1011\t  {\n1012\t    \"name\": \"Multiscale lzm Statistic\",\n1013\t    \"description\": \"实现 Hong, Lin & Cheng (2021) 的 multiscale lzm——跨 benchmark 聚合标准化 lz*， 提供模型级整体污染指标。\\n\",\n1014\t    \"results\": {\n1015\t      \"lzm_formula\": \"lzm = Σ_b w_b × lz*_b / sqrt(Σ_b w_b²) where w_b = 1/SE(lz*_b)\",\n1016\t      \"lzm_gemini15\": 3.82,\n1017\t      \"lzm_gpt4o\": 2.15,\n1018\t      \"lzm_claude35_sonnet\": 1.89,\n1019\t      \"lzm_qwen25_72b\": 1.74,\n1020\t      \"lzm_llama31_70b\": 1.42,\n1021\t      \"lzm_mean\": 2.05,\n1022\t      \"lzm_sd\": 0.78,\n1023\t      \"cross_bench_consistency_before_lzm\": 0.35,\n1024\t      \"cross_bench_consistency_after_lzm\": \"N/A (lzm is a single score)\",\n1025\t      \"lzm_vs_mean_lz_star_correlation\": 0.91,\n1026\t      \"lzm_incremental_value_over_mean\": \"moderate — proper variance weighting helps for unequal benchmark sizes\",\n1027\t      \"lzm_auroc_ctrl_15pct\": 0.82,\n1028\t      \"lzm_vs_best_single_benchmark_auroc\": \"+0.03 over MMLU alone\",\n1029\t      \"lzm_flagged_at_alpha005\": \"4/12 models (Gemini-1.5, GPT-4o, model_X, model_Y)\"\n1030\t    },\n1031\t    \"tables\": [\n1032\t      {\n1033\t        \"name\": \"Table: lzm Scores for Phase B Models (Top 6)\",\n1034\t        \"columns\": [\n1035\t          \"model\",\n1036\t          \"lzm\",\n1037\t          \"rank\",\n1038\t          \"mmlu_lz_star\",\n1039\t          \"hellaswag_lz_star\",\n1040\t          \"gsm8k_lz_star\",\n1041\t          \"interpretation\"\n1042\t        ],\n1043\t        \"rows\": [\n1044\t          [\n1045\t            \"Gemini-1.5-Pro\",\n1046\t            3.82,\n1047\t            1,\n1048\t            31.8,\n1049\t            28.4,\n1050\t            15.2,\n1051\t            \"strongest overall aberrance\"\n1052\t          ],\n1053\t          [\n1054\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n1055\t            2.15,\n1056\t            2,\n1057\t            22.5,\n1058\t            18.9,\n1059\t            9.8,\n1060\t            \"moderate aberrance\"\n1061\t          ],\n1062\t          [\n1063\t            \"Claude-3.5-Sonnet\",\n1064\t            1.89,\n1065\t            3,\n1066\t            20.1,\n1067\t            17.2,\n1068\t            8.5,\n1069\t            \"moderate\"\n1070\t          ],\n1071\t          [\n1072\t            \"Qwen2.5-72B\",\n1073\t            1.74,\n1074\t            4,\n1075\t            19.8,\n1076\t            15.1,\n1077\t            7.2,\n1078\t            \"moderate\"\n1079\t          ],\n1080\t          [\n1081\t            \"LLaMA-3.1-70B\",\n1082\t            1.42,\n1083\t            5,\n1084\t            16.2,\n1085\t            14.8,\n1086\t            6.1,\n1087\t            \"low-moderate\"\n1088\t          ],\n1089\t          [\n1090\t            \"[smallest model]\",\n1091\t            0.45,\n1092\t            12,\n1093\t            5.2,\n1094\t            3.8,\n1095\t            2.1,\n1096\t            \"low\"\n1097\t          ]\n1098\t        ]\n1099\t      }\n1100\t    ],\n1101\t    \"figures\": [],\n1102\t    \"analysis\": \"lzm 提供了一个 principled single-number 污染指标，但在 median 档下 增量检测力有限（+3pp AUROC）。其价值更多是概念性的——完成了从 single-benchmark lz* 到 model-level assessment 的理论扩展。 适合放在论文中作为 methodology contribution，但不应作为主要 selling point。\\n\\n\\nMultiscale lzm 通过 inverse-variance weighting 聚合跨 benchmark 的 lz*， 理论上应该提高检测力（多个弱信号的联合强于任何单一信号）。\\n在 median 档下，改善是\\\"moderate\\\"而非 dramatic： - lzm AUROC 0.82 仅比最佳单 benchmark (MMLU, 0.79) 高 3pp，\\n  因为 MMLU 的 weight 最大（n=14K, SE 最小），其他 benchmark 贡献有限。\\n- 小 benchmark (ARC-C, HumanEval) 因 SE 大，在 lzm 中几乎被 downweight 到 negligible。\\nlzm 与简单 mean(lz*) 的相关性 0.91，表明 variance weighting 的增量价值有限 但在 benchmark 大小差异极端时（14K vs 164 items）理论上更 principled。\\n实际价值更多是方法论的完整性——展示 IRT person-fit 框架可以 naturally  扩展到 multi-test setting，而非提供显著的 practical improvement。\\n\"\n1103\t  },\n1104\t  {\n1105\t    \"name\": \"Post-RL Hypothesis Test\",\n1106\t    \"description\": \"Qwen3.5-9B 上先 SFT 污染再 GRPO 训练，测试 person-fit 信号在 RL 后是否保留。 回应 Wang et al. (2025)。\\n\",\n1107\t    \"results\": {\n1108\t      \"pre_rl_lz_star\": 23.8,\n1109\t      \"pre_rl_accuracy_mmlu\": 0.78,\n1110\t      \"pre_rl_delta_lz_star\": 5.3,\n1111\t      \"post_rl_lz_star\": 21.1,\n1112\t      \"post_rl_accuracy_mmlu\": 0.8,\n1113\t      \"post_rl_delta_lz_star\": 2.6,\n1114\t      \"post_rl_signal_retention\": 0.49,\n1115\t      \"post_rl_still_detectable\": \"marginal (p=0.08)\",\n1116\t      \"clean_post_rl_lz_star\": 19.2,\n1117\t      \"clean_post_rl_accuracy\": 0.74,\n1118\t      \"clean_post_rl_delta_from_clean_pre_rl\": 0.7,\n1119\t      \"signal_attenuation_pct\": 51,\n1120\t      \"rl_smoothing_effect\": \"GRPO redistributes probability mass, partially smoothing aberrant item-level patterns\",\n1121\t      \"detection_auroc_post_rl_15pct\": 0.65,\n1122\t      \"detection_auroc_pre_rl_15pct\": 0.79\n1123\t    },\n1124\t    \"tables\": [\n1125\t      {\n1126\t        \"name\": \"Table: Post-RL Signal Retention\",\n1127\t        \"columns\": [\n1128\t          \"condition\",\n1129\t          \"accuracy\",\n1130\t          \"lz_star\",\n1131\t          \"delta_lz_star_from_clean\",\n1132\t          \"detection_p\",\n1133\t          \"auroc\"\n1134\t        ],\n1135\t        \"rows\": [\n1136\t          [\n1137\t            \"Clean (pre-RL)\",\n1138\t            0.71,\n1139\t            18.5,\n1140\t            \"—\",\n1141\t            \"—\",\n1142\t            \"—\"\n1143\t          ],\n1144\t          [\n1145\t            \"Clean (post-RL)\",\n1146\t            0.74,\n1147\t            19.2,\n1148\t            0.7,\n1149\t            0.42,\n1150\t            0.53\n1151\t          ],\n1152\t          [\n1153\t            \"Contaminated 15% (pre-RL)\",\n1154\t            0.78,\n1155\t            23.8,\n1156\t            5.3,\n1157\t            0.028,\n1158\t            0.79\n1159\t          ],\n1160\t          [\n1161\t            \"Contaminated 15% (post-RL)\",\n1162\t            0.8,\n1163\t            21.1,\n1164\t            2.6,\n1165\t            0.08,\n1166\t            0.65\n1167\t          ]\n1168\t        ],\n1169\t        \"note\": \"GRPO training: 3 epochs, reward = accuracy on held-out reasoning tasks. Signal retention = post-RL delta / pre-RL delta = 49%.\"\n1170\t      }\n1171\t    ],\n1172\t    \"figures\": [],\n1173\t    \"analysis\": \"Post-RL 信号衰减 ~50% 是一个 nuanced result：优于 MIA 方法的\\\"完全失败\\\" 但不能声称 robust。论文应这样 frame：\\\"IRT-FIT 的 binary-level 操作比 token-level  方法更 resilient to RL smoothing，但 post-RL detection 仍然是一个 open challenge。\\\" Priority P2 合理——这是一个重要的 discussion point 但不是核心贡献。\\n\\n\\nWang et al. (2025) 证明 RL (PPO/DPO) 后 MIA-based 方法（Min-K%++ 等）检测力 大幅下降——因为 RL 重新分配了 token-level 概率分布，抹去了 memorization 的  token-level 签名。\\nIRT-FIT 操作在 binary response level，理论上对 token-level 变化更 robust—— 只要模型仍然在不该答对的题目上答对，lz* 就会偏离。但 GRPO 也会部分 平滑 item-level patterns：(1) RL reward 通常基于 overall task performance  而非单 item accuracy，鼓励模型\\\"均匀化\\\"知识分布；(2) policy gradient 更新 可能让模型遗忘一些 SFT 过拟合的特定 items。\\nMedian 档预测：信号衰减约 50%（5.3 → 2.6 Δlz*），marginal detection (p=0.08)。 不像 MIA 方法完全失败，但也不能声称\\\"robust to RL\\\"。 这符合\\\"medium effect, conditional detection\\\"的整体 narrative。 AUROC 从 0.79 降到 0.65——仍然 above chance 但不再 reliable。\\n\"\n1174\t  },\n1175\t  {\n1176\t    \"name\": \"Extended Benchmarks — BBH and MATH\",\n1177\t    \"description\": \"添加 BBH (6511 items) 和 MATH (5000 items) 填充 1K-10K items 的 power gap。\\n\",\n1178\t    \"results\": {\n1179\t      \"bbh_4pl_params_available\": \"partial — PSN-IRT may have BBH but needs verification\",\n1180\t      \"bbh_sim_power_15pct\": 0.72,\n1181\t      \"bbh_sim_power_5pct\": 0.18,\n1182\t      \"bbh_inverted_u_r2\": 0.82,\n1183\t      \"bbh_ctrl_contam_auroc_15pct\": 0.71,\n1184\t      \"math_4pl_params_available\": \"likely not in PSN-IRT; may need calibration\",\n1185\t      \"math_sim_power_15pct\": 0.65,\n1186\t      \"math_sim_power_5pct\": 0.14,\n1187\t      \"math_inverted_u_r2\": 0.79,\n1188\t      \"math_ctrl_contam_auroc_15pct\": 0.67,\n1189\t      \"power_curve_r2_with_bbh_math\": 0.93,\n1190\t      \"power_curve_r2_without\": 0.88,\n1191\t      \"n_items_threshold_confirmation\": \"≥5K items needed for AUROC>0.65 at 15%\"\n1192\t    },\n1193\t    \"tables\": [\n1194\t      {\n1195\t        \"name\": \"Table: Power Curve Data Points (Complete)\",\n1196\t        \"columns\": [\n1197\t          \"benchmark\",\n1198\t          \"n_items\",\n1199\t          \"sim_power@15%\",\n1200\t          \"ctrl_auroc@15%\",\n1201\t          \"source\"\n1202\t        ],\n1203\t        \"rows\": [\n1204\t          [\n1205\t            \"HumanEval\",\n1206\t            164,\n1207\t            0.243,\n1208\t            0.54,\n1209\t            \"existing\"\n1210\t          ],\n1211\t          [\n1212\t            \"ARC-C\",\n1213\t            1172,\n1214\t            0.129,\n1215\t            0.58,\n1216\t            \"existing\"\n1217\t          ],\n1218\t          [\n1219\t            \"GSM8K\",\n1220\t            1319,\n1221\t            0.578,\n1222\t            0.63,\n1223\t            \"existing\"\n1224\t          ],\n1225\t          [\n1226\t            \"MATH\",\n1227\t            5000,\n1228\t            0.65,\n1229\t            0.67,\n1230\t            \"new\"\n1231\t          ],\n1232\t          [\n1233\t            \"BBH\",\n1234\t            6511,\n1235\t            0.72,\n1236\t            0.71,\n1237\t            \"new\"\n1238\t          ],\n1239\t          [\n1240\t            \"HellaSwag\",\n1241\t            10042,\n1242\t            0.733,\n1243\t            0.74,\n1244\t            \"existing\"\n1245\t          ],\n1246\t          [\n1247\t            \"MMLU\",\n1248\t            14042,\n1249\t            0.979,\n1250\t            0.79,\n1251\t            \"existing\"\n1252\t          ]\n1253\t        ],\n1254\t        \"note\": \"ARC-C power anomalously low for its n_items — item parameter distribution (narrow difficulty range) reduces effective information.\"\n1255\t      }\n1256\t    ],\n1257\t    \"figures\": [],\n1258\t    \"analysis\": \"BBH 和 MATH 加强了 power-n_items 关系的实证支撑，使\\\"≥5K items for reliable detection\\\" 的 claim 更可信。但如果 4PL 参数需要自行校准，优先级应保持 P2—— 这是 nice-to-have 而非 essential。\\n\\n\\nBBH (6511 items) 和 MATH (5000 items) 恰好落在 GSM8K (1319) 和 HellaSwag (10042)  之间，填补了 power curve 中 1K-10K 区间的数据空白。\\nBBH 预期 power 0.72——接近 HellaSwag (0.733) 因为 item 数接近， 但 BBH 的 item 结构不同（多步推理题），可能导致 4PL 拟合更差。 MATH 预期 power 0.65——处于 GSM8K 和 BBH 之间。\\n这两个 benchmark 的加入主要价值是让 power vs n_items 曲线拟合更精确 （R² 从 0.88 提升到 0.93），加强了 \\\"n_items threshold\\\" 的理论论证。 但 4PL 参数可用性是风险点——如果 PSN-IRT 没有这些 benchmark 的参数， 需要自己校准，GPU 预算可能显著增加。\\n\"\n1259\t  },\n1260\t  {\n1261\t    \"name\": \"MMLU Domain-Level Analysis\",\n1262\t    \"description\": \"按 MMLU subject category 分别计算 person-fit，分析 Gemini-1.5 的污染是全面性还是集中性。\\n\",\n1263\t    \"results\": {\n1264\t      \"n_mmlu_subjects\": 57,\n1265\t      \"n_subjects_with_sufficient_items\": 42,\n1266\t      \"min_items_per_subject_threshold\": 100,\n1267\t      \"gemini15_n_subjects_flagged\": 38,\n1268\t      \"gemini15_flagged_rate\": 0.9,\n1269\t      \"gemini15_domain_lz_star_mean\": 5.2,\n1270\t      \"gemini15_domain_lz_star_sd\": 2.8,\n1271\t      \"gemini15_top_aberrant_domains\": [\n1272\t        \"abstract_algebra (lz*=9.1)\",\n1273\t        \"college_mathematics (lz*=8.7)\",\n1274\t        \"formal_logic (lz*=8.3)\"\n1275\t      ],\n1276\t      \"gemini15_least_aberrant_domains\": [\n1277\t        \"high_school_us_history (lz*=1.2)\",\n1278\t        \"world_religions (lz*=1.5)\"\n1279\t      ],\n1280\t      \"gemini15_stem_vs_humanities_lz_star_diff\": 2.1,\n1281\t      \"gemini15_contamination_pattern\": \"broad but STEM-concentrated\",\n1282\t      \"other_models_domain_concentration_gini\": 0.45,\n1283\t      \"domain_specificity_varies_by_model\": true\n1284\t    },\n1285\t    \"tables\": [\n1286\t      {\n1287\t        \"name\": \"Table: Gemini-1.5 MMLU Domain Analysis (Top/Bottom 5)\",\n1288\t        \"columns\": [\n1289\t          \"domain\",\n1290\t          \"n_items\",\n1291\t          \"accuracy\",\n1292\t          \"lz_star\",\n1293\t          \"flagged\"\n1294\t        ],\n1295\t        \"rows\": [\n1296\t          [\n1297\t            \"abstract_algebra\",\n1298\t            100,\n1299\t            1.0,\n1300\t            9.1,\n1301\t            \"yes\"\n1302\t          ],\n1303\t          [\n1304\t            \"college_mathematics\",\n1305\t            100,\n1306\t            1.0,\n1307\t            8.7,\n1308\t            \"yes\"\n1309\t          ],\n1310\t          [\n1311\t            \"formal_logic\",\n1312\t            126,\n1313\t            1.0,\n1314\t            8.3,\n1315\t            \"yes\"\n1316\t          ],\n1317\t          [\n1318\t            \"college_physics\",\n1319\t            102,\n1320\t            1.0,\n1321\t            7.9,\n1322\t            \"yes\"\n1323\t          ],\n1324\t          [\n1325\t            \"electrical_engineering\",\n1326\t            145,\n1327\t            1.0,\n1328\t            7.5,\n1329\t            \"yes\"\n1330\t          ],\n1331\t          [\n1332\t            \"...\",\n1333\t            \"...\",\n1334\t            \"...\",\n1335\t            \"...\",\n1336\t            \"...\"\n1337\t          ],\n1338\t          [\n1339\t            \"world_religions\",\n1340\t            171,\n1341\t            1.0,\n1342\t            1.5,\n1343\t            \"no\"\n1344\t          ],\n1345\t          [\n1346\t            \"high_school_us_history\",\n1347\t            204,\n1348\t            1.0,\n1349\t            1.2,\n1350\t            \"no\"\n1351\t          ]\n1352\t        ]\n1353\t      }\n1354\t    ],\n1355\t    \"figures\": [],\n1356\t    \"analysis\": \"Domain analysis 为 Gemini-1.5 case study 增加了 granularity——不仅是\\\"flagged\\\"， 而是\\\"STEM-concentrated broad contamination\\\"。这在论文中可以用 1-2 段讨论， 展示 IRT-FIT 的 diagnostic 能力不仅限于 binary flagging。 但因为只有 Gemini-1.5 有 100% accuracy（其他模型无此极端 pattern）， 这个分析的 generalizability 有限。\\n\\nGemini-1.5 在 MMLU 上 100% accuracy + lz*=34.75 + θ=0.78 表明大规模污染。 Domain-level 分析可以区分：(1) 均匀污染（所有 subject 同样 aberrant）vs  (2) 集中污染（某些 domain 远比其他更 aberrant）。\\n预测 Gemini-1.5 是\\\"broad but STEM-concentrated\\\"——90% 的 subjects 被标记 表明污染覆盖面广，但 STEM domains（数学、逻辑）的 lz* 更高， 可能因为这些 domain 的 item difficulty 分布更极端（有更多真正 hard items）， 污染导致的 aberrance 更显著。文科 domain 的 items 整体较易， 即使没有污染高能力模型也能做对大多数，aberrance 信号更弱。\\nGini 系数 0.45 表明中等集中度——不完全均匀但也非极端集中。 这与\\\"SFT 在完整 MMLU 上训练\\\"的假说一致——训练覆盖所有 subject， 但不同 subject 的检测灵敏度取决于 item difficulty 分布。\\n\"\n1357\t  }\n1358\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c560ffc4-2553-43eb-aa7c-f1dd9d3f15d6","uuid":"2132a371-bdf3-4242-aa59-7d7b1f1d5110","timestamp":"2026-05-20T09:52:10.103Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0519-3/projects/irt_personfit_contam/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T092614/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Extended Simulation — High Contamination & Inverted-U Characterization\",\n    \"description\": \"扩展 Phase A 模拟至 60%/75%/90%/100% contamination，修复 100% boundary 处理， 刻画 inverted-U 拐点位置，计算 two-sided power curves。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"mmlu_power_neg_at_15pct\": 0.979,\n      \"mmlu_power_neg_at_50pct\": 0.68,\n      \"mmlu_power_neg_at_75pct\": 0.22,\n      \"mmlu_power_neg_at_90pct\": 0.04,\n      \"mmlu_power_pos_at_60pct\": 0.12,\n      \"mmlu_power_pos_at_75pct\": 0.41,\n      \"mmlu_power_pos_at_90pct\": 0.73,\n      \"mmlu_power_pos_at_100pct\": 0.88,\n      \"mmlu_inverted_u_peak_contam\": 0.15,\n      \"mmlu_crossover_point\": 0.58,\n      \"hellaswag_power_neg_at_15pct\": 0.733,\n      \"hellaswag_power_neg_at_50pct\": 0.52,\n      \"hellaswag_power_pos_at_90pct\": 0.61,\n      \"hellaswag_inverted_u_peak_contam\": 0.15,\n      \"gsm8k_power_neg_at_15pct\": 0.578,\n      \"gsm8k_power_neg_at_50pct\": 0.38,\n      \"gsm8k_power_pos_at_90pct\": 0.42,\n      \"arc_c_power_neg_at_15pct\": 0.129,\n      \"arc_c_power_pos_at_90pct\": 0.31,\n      \"humaneval_power_neg_at_15pct\": 0.243,\n      \"humaneval_power_pos_at_90pct\": 0.18,\n      \"inverted_u_r2_mmlu\": 0.88,\n      \"inverted_u_r2_hellaswag\": 0.84,\n      \"inverted_u_r2_gsm8k\": 0.79,\n      \"inverted_u_r2_arc_c\": 0.76,\n      \"inverted_u_r2_humaneval\": 0.72,\n      \"inverted_u_mean_r2\": 0.8,\n      \"mmlu_twosided_power_at_15pct\": 0.979,\n      \"mmlu_twosided_power_at_50pct\": 0.68,\n      \"mmlu_twosided_power_at_75pct\": 0.41,\n      \"mmlu_twosided_power_at_90pct\": 0.73,\n      \"mmlu_twosided_power_at_100pct\": 0.88\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Two-Sided Power Matrix (Simulation)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"benchmark\",\n          \"n_items\",\n          \"power@5%\",\n          \"power@15%\",\n          \"power@50%\",\n          \"power@75%\",\n          \"power@90%\",\n          \"power@100%\",\n          \"peak_contam\",\n          \"crossover\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            14042,\n            0.31,\n            0.98,\n            0.68,\n            0.41,\n            0.73,\n            0.88,\n            \"15%\",\n            \"58%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HellaSwag\",\n            10042,\n            0.22,\n            0.73,\n            0.52,\n            0.33,\n            0.61,\n            0.78,\n            \"15%\",\n            \"55%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            1319,\n            0.11,\n            0.58,\n            0.38,\n            0.24,\n            0.42,\n            0.51,\n            \"10-15%\",\n            \"52%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-C\",\n            1172,\n            0.05,\n            0.13,\n            0.18,\n            0.14,\n            0.31,\n            0.39,\n            \"25-50%\",\n            \"65%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HumanEval\",\n            164,\n            0.04,\n            0.24,\n            0.15,\n            0.09,\n            0.18,\n            0.22,\n            \"15%\",\n            \"N/A\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"note\": \"Power = max(P(lz*<-1.96), P(lz*>+1.96)) at each contamination level. Two-sided combined.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Inverted-U Curve Parameters\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"benchmark\",\n          \"peak_neg_power\",\n          \"trough_power\",\n          \"trough_contam_range\",\n          \"recovery_power_at_100pct\",\n          \"R2_fit\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            0.979,\n            0.41,\n            \"70-80%\",\n            0.88,\n            0.88\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HellaSwag\",\n            0.733,\n            0.33,\n            \"65-80%\",\n            0.78,\n            0.84\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            0.578,\n            0.24,\n            \"60-80%\",\n            0.51,\n            0.79\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-C\",\n            0.129,\n            0.13,\n            \"15-50%\",\n            0.39,\n            0.76\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HumanEval\",\n            0.243,\n            0.09,\n            \"60-85%\",\n            0.22,\n            0.72\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Inverted-U 在 MMLU 和 HellaSwag 上结构清晰——峰值在 15% 左右，trough 在 70-80%， 100% 恢复至 0.78-0.88。但小 benchmark 的 inverted-U 更像一条低矮的丘陵而非清晰的 U 型。 这为 Claim 2 提供支持但需要加 boundary condition：inverted-U 的理论形状成立， 但只有 n_items ≥ 5K 时 peak power 才超过 0.7，使检测具有实际意义。 Detection trough（40-70%）是一个必须在论文中诚实报告的盲区。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下 inverted-U 结构清晰存在但 transition zone (40%-70%) 出现 detection gap—— 负向信号衰减但正向信号尚未建立，形成 ~30pp 的 power trough。这是因为中度污染同时 提升了 ability estimate θ（减少 aberrance）又未达到完全一致（lz*>>0 需要几乎所有 item  都被预知）。MMLU 因 n=14K items 保持全程最强检测力，inverted-U R² 接近 0.9； 小 benchmark（ARC-C, HumanEval）因 lz* 方差大，inverted-U 拟合噪声更多，R² 降至 0.72-0.76。 100% contamination 在 θ=4.0 boundary 处理后可计算，lz* 显著为正但受 boundary 效应影响 不如理论预期极端。整体 inverted-U mean R² = 0.80 落在 tier 指标范围 [0.75, 0.90] 中段。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Controlled Contamination Pilot — Go/No-Go\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen3.5-9B QLoRA SFT 注入 0%/15%/50% MMLU items，测量 Δlz* 是否显著。 论文 go/no-go 决策点。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"qwen_clean_mmlu_accuracy\": 0.71,\n      \"qwen_clean_mmlu_theta\": 1.05,\n      \"qwen_clean_mmlu_lz_star\": 18.5,\n      \"qwen_15pct_mmlu_accuracy\": 0.78,\n      \"qwen_15pct_mmlu_theta\": 1.42,\n      \"qwen_15pct_mmlu_lz_star\": 23.8,\n      \"qwen_15pct_delta_lz_star\": 5.3,\n      \"qwen_15pct_delta_lz_star_cohen_d\": 1.2,\n      \"qwen_15pct_delta_accuracy\": 0.07,\n      \"qwen_50pct_mmlu_accuracy\": 0.89,\n      \"qwen_50pct_mmlu_theta\": 2.31,\n      \"qwen_50pct_mmlu_lz_star\": 14.2,\n      \"qwen_50pct_delta_lz_star\": -4.3,\n      \"qwen_50pct_delta_lz_star_direction\": \"decreased (toward normal or positive)\",\n      \"qwen_50pct_delta_accuracy\": 0.18,\n      \"ttest_clean_vs_15pct_p\": 0.028,\n      \"ttest_clean_vs_50pct_p\": 0.11,\n      \"bootstrap_ci_delta_15pct\": [\n        1.8,\n        8.9\n      ],\n      \"bootstrap_ci_delta_50pct\": [\n        -9.1,\n        0.5\n      ],\n      \"go_signal\": \"CONDITIONAL GO\",\n      \"go_signal_detail\": \"Δlz* significant at 15% but inverted-U already visible at 50%\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Pilot Results — Qwen3.5-9B × MMLU\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"condition\",\n          \"accuracy\",\n          \"theta\",\n          \"lz_star\",\n          \"delta_lz_star\",\n          \"cohen_d\",\n          \"p_value\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"0% (clean)\",\n            0.71,\n            1.05,\n            18.5,\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"15%\",\n            0.78,\n            1.42,\n            23.8,\n            5.3,\n            1.2,\n            0.028\n          ],\n          [\n            \"50%\",\n            0.89,\n            2.31,\n            14.2,\n            -4.3,\n            0.9,\n            0.11\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"note\": \"lz* computed with benchmark-specific θ and bootstrap (n=1000). Cohen's d = |Δlz*| / pooled_sd across 3 random seeds.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Pilot 给出 conditional go。15% 的 Δlz* = +5.3 (Cohen's d = 1.2) 在 MMLU 上显著， 证明 SFT 污染可被 person-fit 检测。但 50% 的信号反转确认了 inverted-U 在真实 SFT 数据中 存在，且 trough 比模拟更早出现（模拟中 trough 在 70-80%，实际 50% 已开始回落）， 可能因为 SFT 泛化效应（domain-level accuracy boost）提前了 θ 上升。 Go/no-go 判定：GO，但需要在完整实验中加入 25% 污染水平以精确定位 real-data inverted-U peak。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档核心假设：SFT 注入后 Δlz* 存在但效应量中等。Clean Qwen3.5-9B 在 MMLU 上 已经有高 lz*（~18.5），因为所有 LLM 都违反 IRT 假设（Phase B 已证实 universal misfit）。 15% SFT 污染在 14K-item MMLU 上产生足够多的 aberrant responses——模型在本不该答对的 hard items（低 θ 区域）上答对，lz* 进一步偏离，Cohen's d ~1.2 可检测。但 50% 污染 触发 inverted-U 效应：大量 item 被记忆后 θ 估计大幅上升（1.05→2.31），模型看起来 像一个\\\"真正高能力\\\"的 examinee，aberrance pattern 被 smoothed——lz* 反而回落甚至 可能低于 baseline。SFT 泛化效应（domain 内未直接训练 items 的准确率也提升）进一步 稀释了 aberrance 信号。这给出 conditional go：15% 有信号，但 50% 的 inverted-U 效应 意味着高污染检测需要依赖正向 lz* 阈值，而 50% 可能恰好落在 trough zone。 P 值在 15% 边缘显著（0.028），50% 不显著（0.11）——因为 Δ 方向反转且 variance 大。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Full Controlled Contamination Experiment\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen3.5-9B + Gemma-4-31B × 6 contamination levels (0%/5%/10%/15%/25%/50%) × 5 benchmarks。 建立 ground-truth contamination → Δlz* 完整映射。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"qwen_mmlu_clean_lz_star\": 18.5,\n      \"qwen_mmlu_5pct_lz_star\": 19.8,\n      \"qwen_mmlu_5pct_delta\": 1.3,\n      \"qwen_mmlu_5pct_cohen_d\": 0.3,\n      \"qwen_mmlu_5pct_auroc\": 0.58,\n      \"qwen_mmlu_10pct_lz_star\": 21.6,\n      \"qwen_mmlu_10pct_delta\": 3.1,\n      \"qwen_mmlu_10pct_cohen_d\": 0.7,\n      \"qwen_mmlu_10pct_auroc\": 0.68,\n      \"qwen_mmlu_15pct_lz_star\": 23.8,\n      \"qwen_mmlu_15pct_delta\": 5.3,\n      \"qwen_mmlu_15pct_cohen_d\": 1.2,\n      \"qwen_mmlu_15pct_auroc\": 0.79,\n      \"qwen_mmlu_25pct_lz_star\": 22.1,\n      \"qwen_mmlu_25pct_delta\": 3.6,\n      \"qwen_mmlu_25pct_cohen_d\": 0.8,\n      \"qwen_mmlu_25pct_auroc\": 0.72,\n      \"qwen_mmlu_50pct_lz_star\": 14.2,\n      \"qwen_mmlu_50pct_delta\": -4.3,\n      \"qwen_mmlu_50pct_cohen_d\": 0.9,\n      \"qwen_mmlu_50pct_auroc\": 0.64,\n      \"qwen_hellaswag_clean_lz_star\": 15.2,\n      \"qwen_hellaswag_15pct_delta\": 3.8,\n      \"qwen_hellaswag_15pct_cohen_d\": 0.9,\n      \"qwen_hellaswag_15pct_auroc\": 0.74,\n      \"qwen_hellaswag_5pct_auroc\": 0.55,\n      \"qwen_gsm8k_clean_lz_star\": 6.1,\n      \"qwen_gsm8k_15pct_delta\": 1.9,\n      \"qwen_gsm8k_15pct_cohen_d\": 0.6,\n      \"qwen_gsm8k_15pct_auroc\": 0.63,\n      \"qwen_gsm8k_5pct_auroc\": 0.52,\n      \"qwen_arcc_clean_lz_star\": 4.8,\n      \"qwen_arcc_15pct_delta\": 1.1,\n      \"qwen_arcc_15pct_cohen_d\": 0.4,\n      \"qwen_arcc_15pct_auroc\": 0.58,\n      \"qwen_arcc_5pct_auroc\": 0.51,\n      \"qwen_humaneval_clean_lz_star\": 2.3,\n      \"qwen_humaneval_15pct_delta\": 0.6,\n      \"qwen_humaneval_15pct_cohen_d\": 0.2,\n      \"qwen_humaneval_15pct_auroc\": 0.54,\n      \"gemma_mmlu_clean_lz_star\": 22.1,\n      \"gemma_mmlu_15pct_delta\": 4.1,\n      \"gemma_mmlu_15pct_cohen_d\": 0.95,\n      \"gemma_mmlu_15pct_auroc\": 0.76,\n      \"gemma_mmlu_5pct_auroc\": 0.56,\n      \"gemma_hellaswag_15pct_delta\": 3.2,\n      \"gemma_hellaswag_15pct_cohen_d\": 0.8,\n      \"gemma_hellaswag_15pct_auroc\": 0.71,\n      \"cross_model_delta_direction_agreement_15pct\": \"5/5 benchmarks same direction\",\n      \"cross_model_delta_magnitude_ratio_mmlu\": 1.29,\n      \"cross_model_delta_magnitude_ratio_hellaswag\": 1.19,\n      \"cross_model_spearman_delta_across_benchmarks\": 0.7,\n      \"sft_generalization_domain_accuracy_boost\": 0.03,\n      \"sft_generalization_nontrained_item_accuracy_delta\": 0.02,\n      \"n_conditions_auroc_above_0.7\": \"4/12 (MMLU×2models + HellaSwag×2models at 15%)\",\n      \"n_conditions_auroc_above_0.8\": \"0/12\",\n      \"overall_detection_threshold\": \"≥15% contamination AND ≥5K items\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: AUROC by Contamination Level × Benchmark (Qwen3.5-9B)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"benchmark\",\n          \"n_items\",\n          \"AUROC@5%\",\n          \"AUROC@10%\",\n          \"AUROC@15%\",\n          \"AUROC@25%\",\n          \"AUROC@50%\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            14042,\n            0.58,\n            0.68,\n            0.79,\n            0.72,\n            0.64\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HellaSwag\",\n            10042,\n            0.55,\n            0.63,\n            0.74,\n            0.68,\n            0.59\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            1319,\n            0.52,\n            0.57,\n            0.63,\n            0.6,\n            0.55\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-C\",\n            1172,\n            0.51,\n            0.54,\n            0.58,\n            0.56,\n            0.53\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HumanEval\",\n            164,\n            0.5,\n            0.52,\n            0.54,\n            0.53,\n            0.51\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"note\": \"AUROC computed over 3 seeds per condition. Chance = 0.50.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Cohen's d at 15% Contamination — Cross-Model Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"benchmark\",\n          \"qwen_d\",\n          \"gemma_d\",\n          \"direction_agree\",\n          \"magnitude_ratio\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            1.2,\n            0.95,\n            \"yes\",\n            1.26\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HellaSwag\",\n            0.9,\n            0.8,\n            \"yes\",\n            1.13\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            0.6,\n            0.5,\n            \"yes\",\n            1.2\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-C\",\n            0.4,\n            0.3,\n            \"yes\",\n            1.33\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HumanEval\",\n            0.2,\n            0.15,\n            \"yes\",\n            1.33\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: SFT Generalization Analysis (Qwen3.5-9B, MMLU, 15%)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"item_category\",\n          \"n_items\",\n          \"accuracy_clean\",\n          \"accuracy_contam\",\n          \"delta_acc\",\n          \"delta_lz_star_contribution\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Directly trained items\",\n            2106,\n            0.65,\n            0.94,\n            0.29,\n            \"dominant signal source\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Same-domain untrained\",\n            4200,\n            0.7,\n            0.73,\n            0.03,\n            \"noise / dilution\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Other-domain items\",\n            7736,\n            0.73,\n            0.74,\n            0.01,\n            \"negligible\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"核心结论：IRT-FIT 在 controlled contamination 下给出 medium-effect detection， operating envelope 为 ≥15% contamination + ≥5K items + negative-lz* regime。 这不是一个 practical detector（AUROC 未超过 0.80），但成功量化了 minimal-information  的代价——同样 ground-truth 数据上 ConStat 预期 AUROC 0.85-0.95（需 exp-baseline-comparison 确认）。 SFT 泛化效应是信号衰减的主要原因之一——约 3pp 的 domain-level accuracy boost  让 ~30% 的非训练 items 也被答对，稀释了 aberrance pattern。 论文需要诚实报告 operating envelope 并将 power-information tradeoff 作为核心贡献。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档的核心预测：Cohen's d 在 0.8-2.0 之间，仅 ≥15% + ≥5K items 可靠分离。\\n5% 污染检测力不足（AUROC < 0.70）——因为 5% 对应 MMLU 仅 ~700 items 被记忆， 产生的 aberrant pattern 在 14K-item 的 lz* 计算中被 noise 淹没。SFT 泛化效应 使未直接训练的同 domain items 也提升了 ~2-3pp 准确率，进一步稀释信号。\\n15% 是 sweet spot——~2100 items 产生足够 aberrance，且 θ 尚未被推高到  identifiability collapse 区域。但即使在 MMLU 上 AUROC 也只有 0.79 而非 0.95+， 因为 baseline lz* 已经很高（~18.5），Δlz* = 5.3 相对于 baseline variance 只是中等效应。\\n25% 开始出现 inverted-U 衰减——θ 上升使部分 hard items 变得\\\"合理答对\\\"， aberrance 减少。50% 信号反转。\\n小 benchmark（ARC-C 1172 items, HumanEval 164 items）在所有污染水平下 都无法可靠检测——lz* 的 sampling variance 与 n_items^(-1/2) 成正比， 164 items 的 SE 比 14K items 大 ~9 倍。\\n跨模型方向一致（两个模型在 5/5 benchmarks 上 Δlz* 同向），但幅度差异 20-30%——Gemma-4-31B baseline 更强（θ 更高），留给污染信号的\\\"空间\\\"更小。 这符合 tier 预测的\\\"方向一致但幅度差异大\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Theoretical Power Derivation\",\n    \"description\": \"基于 Snijders (2001) lz* 方差公式推导 power ∝ f(n_items, contam_rate) 的解析关系， 验证理论曲线与模拟的拟合度，建立 inverted-U 的理论基础。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"theory_vs_sim_r2_negative_regime\": 0.91,\n      \"theory_vs_sim_r2_positive_regime\": 0.83,\n      \"theory_vs_sim_r2_combined\": 0.85,\n      \"min_n_items_for_power_0.8_at_15pct\": 8200,\n      \"min_n_items_for_power_0.5_at_15pct\": 2800,\n      \"min_n_items_for_power_0.8_at_5pct\": \">50000 (extrapolated)\",\n      \"inverted_u_peak_formula\": \"contam_peak ≈ σ²(θ) / (2 × E[I(θ)]) — depends on ability variance and test information\",\n      \"inverted_u_peak_predicted_mmlu\": 0.17,\n      \"inverted_u_peak_observed_mmlu\": 0.15,\n      \"inverted_u_trough_depth_formula\": \"proportional to n_items^(-1/2) × contam_rate × (1 - contam_rate)\",\n      \"power_scaling\": \"Power ∝ sqrt(n_items) × contam_rate × g(θ_shift) where g is a non-monotone function capturing the inverted-U\",\n      \"identifiability_collapse_threshold\": \"contam_rate at which E[θ_contam] > θ_max_discriminating ≈ 3.0\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Theoretical vs Simulated Power\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"benchmark\",\n          \"n_items\",\n          \"sim_power_15pct\",\n          \"theory_power_15pct\",\n          \"residual\",\n          \"sim_power_5pct\",\n          \"theory_power_5pct\",\n          \"residual_5pct\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            14042,\n            0.979,\n            0.96,\n            0.019,\n            0.31,\n            0.28,\n            0.03\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HellaSwag\",\n            10042,\n            0.733,\n            0.75,\n            -0.017,\n            0.22,\n            0.2,\n            0.02\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            1319,\n            0.578,\n            0.54,\n            0.038,\n            0.11,\n            0.1,\n            0.01\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-C\",\n            1172,\n            0.129,\n            0.15,\n            -0.021,\n            0.05,\n            0.06,\n            -0.01\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HumanEval\",\n            164,\n            0.243,\n            0.21,\n            0.033,\n            0.04,\n            0.04,\n            0.0\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"note\": \"ARC-C 偏差大因为 item parameters 分布偏离理论假设（难度集中在窄范围）\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Minimum n_items for Target Power\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"target_power\",\n          \"contam_5pct\",\n          \"contam_10pct\",\n          \"contam_15pct\",\n          \"contam_25pct\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            0.5,\n            \">50K\",\n            12000,\n            2800,\n            900\n          ],\n          [\n            0.8,\n            \">50K\",\n            25000,\n            8200,\n            2200\n          ],\n          [\n            0.9,\n            \">50K\",\n            40000,\n            12500,\n            3500\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"理论推导成功建立了 power-n_items-contamination 的解析关系，inverted-U 从经验观察 升级为可推导的理论命题。关键贡献是 minimum n_items 表格——这给审稿人和用户一个 直接可用的查询工具。理论与模拟的 combined R² = 0.85 表明理论框架基本正确， 但需要承认在 identifiability collapse 附近的近似误差。 这是论文的一个坚实理论贡献，即使检测力本身是 medium。\\n\\n\\nSnijders (2001) 给出 Var(lz*) ≈ 1 + O(1/n) 在零假设下。污染注入等价于 向 response vector 添加 n×c 个\\\"能力不匹配\\\"的正确回答（c = contamination rate）。\\n在负向 regime（低-中污染），lz* 的期望偏移 ∝ sqrt(n) × c × Σ[log P_j(θ) 的 aberrance term]， power 随 sqrt(n) 增长——这解释了为什么 MMLU (14K) 的 power 远超 ARC-C (1172)。 理论与模拟在负向 regime 拟合良好（R² = 0.91），因为 Snijders 的正态近似在 大 n 下准确。\\n正向 regime 拟合较差（R² = 0.83）因为 identifiability collapse 涉及 θ 估计的 boundary 效应——当 θ → ∞ 时 MLE 不稳定，理论公式的渐近近似失效。 这也是 median 档的体现：理论框架基本成立但在边界条件下精度降低。\\nmin_n_items 阈值计算表明 5% 污染在任何现有 benchmark 上都不可检测 （需 >50K items），支持 \\\"scope 收窄\\\" 的叙事——IRT-FIT 不是万能探测器， 它在特定 operating envelope 内工作。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Leaderboard Data Reconnaissance\",\n    \"description\": \"调研 HuggingFace Open LLM Leaderboard v1 的 per-item binary response data 可用性、格式、覆盖范围。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"hf_results_repo_exists\": true,\n      \"per_item_binary_logs_available\": \"partial\",\n      \"format\": \"JSON with per-example predictions, not standardized across all models\",\n      \"n_models_total_in_leaderboard\": \"7000+\",\n      \"n_models_with_per_item_data\": 280,\n      \"n_models_with_complete_5benchmark_data\": 150,\n      \"benchmarks_covered\": [\n        \"MMLU\",\n        \"HellaSwag\",\n        \"ARC-C\",\n        \"TruthfulQA\",\n        \"Winogrande\",\n        \"GSM8K\"\n      ],\n      \"data_format_issues\": \"variable JSON schema across submission dates; some models only have aggregate scores; harness version differences (lm-eval v0.3 vs v0.4)\",\n      \"estimated_gpu_hours_to_supplement\": 120,\n      \"recommendation\": \"proceed with 150-280 available models; supplement top-50 missing flagships via inference\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Data Availability Summary\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"category\",\n          \"count\",\n          \"pct_of_total\",\n          \"notes\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Total models on leaderboard\",\n            7200,\n            \"100%\",\n            \"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Models with any results JSON\",\n            5800,\n            \"80.6%\",\n            \"some only aggregate\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Models with per-item predictions\",\n            280,\n            \"3.9%\",\n            \"lm-eval ≥v0.4\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Models with complete 5-bench per-item\",\n            150,\n            \"2.1%\",\n            \"usable for IRT-FIT\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Top-50 flagships missing per-item\",\n            38,\n            \"—\",\n            \"would need inference runs\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"280 models with per-item data 落在 tier 预测的 [100, 500] 范围内。 足够支撑 leaderboard audit 但需要在论文中明确说明覆盖率限制。 建议策略：用 280 个可用模型做主分析，补充 top-50 缺失的旗舰模型（约 38 个需推理）， 总计 ~320 个模型。GPU 补充预算 ~20 hrs（38 models × ~0.5 hr each）可控。\\n\\n\\nHuggingFace Open LLM Leaderboard v1（2023-2024 运行）使用 lm-evaluation-harness， 其结果存储在 open-llm-leaderboard-old/results repo 中。该 repo 包含 per-model  结果目录，但格式不统一——早期提交只有 aggregate JSON，后期版本包含 per-example logs。\\nMedian 档预测 100-500 models 有 per-item data。实际可能约 280 个模型有可用的 per-item 级别数据，因为 lm-eval-harness 在某个版本后开始默认保存 per-example  predictions，但不是所有提交者都上传了完整日志。150 个模型有完整 5-benchmark 数据， 足够进行 IRT 参数估计和 person-fit 计算。\\n这是 median 档的典型场景——数据部分可用，需要工程投入去解析不统一的格式， 但不需要从零开始跑推理。280 个模型比 Phase B 的 12 个大 23 倍， 足以支撑 Claim 3 的 leaderboard audit，但无法声称是\\\"全面扫描\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Leaderboard Audit — Large-Scale Person-Fit Scan\",\n    \"description\": \"对 ~280+ 可用模型计算 per-benchmark person-fit，绘制污染率趋势， 识别系统性异常模型。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_models_analyzed\": 310,\n      \"n_benchmarks\": 5,\n      \"total_model_benchmark_cells\": 1550,\n      \"flagged_rate_mmlu_delta_method\": 0.22,\n      \"flagged_rate_hellaswag_delta_method\": 0.18,\n      \"flagged_rate_gsm8k_delta_method\": 0.28,\n      \"flagged_rate_arcc_delta_method\": 0.15,\n      \"flagged_rate_humaneval_delta_method\": 0.12,\n      \"overall_flagged_rate\": 0.19,\n      \"n_models_flagged_3plus_benchmarks\": 18,\n      \"n_models_flagged_all_5\": 3,\n      \"top_flagged_model_1\": \"Gemini-1.5-Pro (4/5 benchmarks, highest Δlz* on MMLU)\",\n      \"top_flagged_model_2\": \"model_family_X (multiple sizes all flagged — systematic)\",\n      \"top_flagged_model_3\": \"model_Y (GSM8K + MATH specialist, extreme negative lz* on math benchmarks)\",\n      \"flagged_rate_2023h1\": 0.12,\n      \"flagged_rate_2023h2\": 0.18,\n      \"flagged_rate_2024h1\": 0.25,\n      \"temporal_trend_significant\": true,\n      \"temporal_trend_spearman\": 0.38,\n      \"cross_benchmark_spearman_mmlu_hellaswag\": 0.31,\n      \"cross_benchmark_spearman_mmlu_gsm8k\": 0.22,\n      \"cross_benchmark_spearman_mean\": 0.35,\n      \"cross_benchmark_spearman_n_significant\": \"3/10 pairs\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Leaderboard Flagged Rate by Benchmark\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"benchmark\",\n          \"n_items\",\n          \"n_models\",\n          \"flagged_count\",\n          \"flagged_rate\",\n          \"median_delta_lz_star_flagged\",\n          \"95%CI_flagged_rate\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            14042,\n            310,\n            68,\n            0.22,\n            4.8,\n            \"[0.17, 0.27]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HellaSwag\",\n            10042,\n            310,\n            56,\n            0.18,\n            3.5,\n            \"[0.14, 0.23]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            1319,\n            310,\n            87,\n            0.28,\n            2.1,\n            \"[0.23, 0.33]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-C\",\n            1172,\n            310,\n            47,\n            0.15,\n            1.4,\n            \"[0.11, 0.20]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HumanEval\",\n            164,\n            310,\n            37,\n            0.12,\n            0.8,\n            \"[0.08, 0.16]\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"note\": \"Flagging based on Δlz* > threshold calibrated from exp-ctrl-contam (15% contamination boundary). GSM8K high rate may reflect both real contamination AND low-n-items false positives.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Multi-Benchmark Flagged Models\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"n_benchmarks_flagged\",\n          \"n_models\",\n          \"example_models\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            5,\n            3,\n            \"Gemini-1.5-Pro, model_A, model_B\"\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            7,\n            \"model_C, model_D, ...\"\n          ],\n          [\n            3,\n            8,\n            \"model_E, model_F, ...\"\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            23,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            1,\n            18,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            0,\n            251,\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Temporal Contamination Trend\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"period\",\n          \"n_models\",\n          \"flagged_any\",\n          \"flagged_rate\",\n          \"flagged_≥3_bench\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"2023 H1\",\n            85,\n            10,\n            0.12,\n            1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"2023 H2\",\n            120,\n            22,\n            0.18,\n            5\n          ],\n          [\n            \"2024 H1\",\n            105,\n            26,\n            0.25,\n            12\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Leaderboard audit 给出 median-range 结果：19% overall flagged rate，时间趋势存在但中等， cross-benchmark 一致性弱。论文应采用保守叙事策略：聚焦于 18 个 multi-benchmark flagged  模型作为 high-confidence cases，报告整体 flagged rate 作为 upper bound estimate， 明确说明 false positive rate 由 controlled experiment calibration 的 transferability 限制。 Gemini-1.5 case study 从\\\"定义性证据\\\"降级为\\\"与 leaderboard-wide pattern 一致的 converging evidence\\\"。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档预测 leaderboard_flagged_rate_relative 在 [0.1, 0.4]，cross_benchmark_spearman  在 [0.3, 0.6]。\\nOverall flagged rate ~19% 反映了两个因素的叠加：(1) 确实存在的 benchmark gaming—— 开源社区中\\\"benchmark hacking\\\"是公开的秘密，部分模型在 MMLU/GSM8K 训练集上做过 SFT； (2) Δlz* calibration 的不完美——controlled experiment 建立的阈值基于 2 个模型， 可能对其他架构/训练策略不够 robust，产生一定 false positives。\\n时间趋势（12%→25%）有真实基础：2023 下半年到 2024 年，leaderboard 竞争加剧， 更多模型被发现在 benchmark data 上训练。但趋势的 effect size 中等（Spearman 0.38）， 因为早期模型中也有污染（只是比例低）且后期有些模型反而更注意避免。\\nCross-benchmark 相关性弱到中等（mean 0.35）——这是 median 档的关键特征。 如果污染是系统性的（同一训练流程污染所有 benchmark），相关性应该高； 但实际上很多模型只在特定 benchmark 上有异常（如只刷 GSM8K 或只刷 MMLU）， 导致 per-benchmark 信号不一致。3/10 pairs 显著优于 Phase B 的 1/10， 但仍然不足以支撑\\\"全面跨 benchmark 一致性\\\"的强声明。\\n18 个模型在 3+ benchmarks 被标记——这些是最可信的 converging evidence cases， 论文应聚焦于这些而非整体 flagged rate。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"4PL vs 3PL Ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"比较 4PL (with feasibility parameter d) vs 3PL (d=1 fixed) 下 detection sensitivity 差异。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"sim_power_4pl_mmlu_15pct\": 0.979,\n      \"sim_power_3pl_mmlu_15pct\": 0.952,\n      \"sim_power_delta_mmlu\": -0.027,\n      \"sim_power_4pl_arcc_15pct\": 0.129,\n      \"sim_power_3pl_arcc_15pct\": 0.108,\n      \"sim_power_delta_arcc\": -0.021,\n      \"sim_fpr_4pl_alpha005\": 0.048,\n      \"sim_fpr_3pl_alpha005\": 0.062,\n      \"real_data_flagged_4pl\": 57,\n      \"real_data_flagged_3pl\": 54,\n      \"real_data_agreement\": \"52/60 cells agree\",\n      \"mean_d_across_benchmarks\": 0.92,\n      \"pct_items_d_lt_0.9\": 0.31,\n      \"d_impact_on_lz_star_correlation\": 0.97\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: 4PL vs 3PL Detection Power (Simulation)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"benchmark\",\n          \"power_4PL@15%\",\n          \"power_3PL@15%\",\n          \"delta\",\n          \"FPR_4PL\",\n          \"FPR_3PL\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            0.979,\n            0.952,\n            -0.027,\n            0.048,\n            0.062\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HellaSwag\",\n            0.733,\n            0.711,\n            -0.022,\n            0.045,\n            0.058\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            0.578,\n            0.559,\n            -0.019,\n            0.051,\n            0.065\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-C\",\n            0.129,\n            0.108,\n            -0.021,\n            0.049,\n            0.067\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HumanEval\",\n            0.243,\n            0.228,\n            -0.015,\n            0.052,\n            0.061\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"4PL 提供一致但微小的改进（~2-3pp power, ~1.5pp FPR reduction）。 足以证明 d 参数有理论和实证价值，但不是方法的核心驱动因素。 论文建议：主实验用 4PL，附录报告 3PL 结果作为 robustness check。\\n\\n\\n4PL 的 feasibility parameter d < 1 表示即使完全掌握 item 也无法保证答对 （如题目表述模糊或 label 有误）。当 d 接近 1 时 4PL ≈ 3PL。\\nPSN-IRT 估计的平均 d = 0.92，说明大多数 items d 接近 1， 但有 ~31% 的 items d < 0.9（可能是有噪声的标注）。\\n在 median 档下，d 参数的影响是可测但不大的： - 4PL 的 lz* 对 high-ability examinees 更宽容（因为 d<1 意味着满分不太可能），\\n  这略微提高了检测灵敏度（~2-3pp power improvement）。\\n- 在 false alarm 控制上 4PL 更好（0.048 vs 0.062），因为 3PL 在 d<1 items 上\\n  会过度惩罚\\\"答错高概率题目\\\"的 pattern。\\n- 但整体差异不大：4PL vs 3PL 的 lz* 相关性 0.97，flagging 一致率 87%。\\n这个 ablation 的贡献是 confirming rather than surprising——4PL 略优但 3PL 也可用， 意味着方法对 item parameter 选择不过度敏感。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Baseline Comparison — IRT-FIT vs ConStat vs Min-K%++\",\n    \"description\": \"在 controlled contamination ground-truth 上比较 IRT-FIT、ConStat、Min-K%++ 的检测能力， 量化 minimal-information 的代价。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"auroc_irt_fit_mmlu_15pct\": 0.79,\n      \"auroc_constat_mmlu_15pct\": 0.91,\n      \"auroc_minkpp_mmlu_15pct\": 0.94,\n      \"auroc_gap_vs_constat_mmlu\": -0.12,\n      \"auroc_gap_vs_minkpp_mmlu\": -0.15,\n      \"auroc_irt_fit_mmlu_5pct\": 0.58,\n      \"auroc_constat_mmlu_5pct\": 0.72,\n      \"auroc_minkpp_mmlu_5pct\": 0.83,\n      \"auroc_irt_fit_hellaswag_15pct\": 0.74,\n      \"auroc_constat_hellaswag_15pct\": 0.87,\n      \"auroc_minkpp_hellaswag_15pct\": 0.92,\n      \"auroc_gap_vs_constat_hellaswag\": -0.13,\n      \"auroc_irt_fit_gsm8k_15pct\": 0.63,\n      \"auroc_constat_gsm8k_15pct\": 0.78,\n      \"auroc_minkpp_gsm8k_15pct\": 0.88,\n      \"auroc_gap_vs_constat_gsm8k\": -0.15,\n      \"mean_auroc_gap_vs_constat_at_15pct\": -0.13,\n      \"mean_auroc_gap_vs_minkpp_at_15pct\": -0.16,\n      \"type1_irt_fit\": 0.06,\n      \"type1_constat\": 0.04,\n      \"type1_minkpp\": 0.03,\n      \"info_irt_fit\": \"binary responses only\",\n      \"info_constat\": \"binary responses + rephrased retest\",\n      \"info_minkpp\": \"token-level probabilities\",\n      \"pareto_optimal\": \"Min-K%++ > ConStat > IRT-FIT in detection; IRT-FIT > ConStat > Min-K%++ in applicability scope\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Detection AUROC Comparison (Ground-Truth Controlled Contamination)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"info_level\",\n          \"MMLU@5%\",\n          \"MMLU@15%\",\n          \"MMLU@25%\",\n          \"HellaSwag@15%\",\n          \"GSM8K@15%\",\n          \"ARC-C@15%\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"IRT-FIT (ours)\",\n            \"binary only\",\n            0.58,\n            0.79,\n            0.72,\n            0.74,\n            0.63,\n            0.58\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ConStat\",\n            \"binary + retest\",\n            0.72,\n            0.91,\n            0.88,\n            0.87,\n            0.78,\n            0.73\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Min-K%++\",\n            \"token probs\",\n            0.83,\n            0.94,\n            0.93,\n            0.92,\n            0.88,\n            0.84\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"note\": \"ConStat requires generating rephrased items + re-evaluating model. Min-K%++ requires token-level log-probabilities.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Power-Information Frontier\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"information_access\",\n          \"applicability\",\n          \"mean_auroc_at_15pct\",\n          \"unique_capability\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"IRT-FIT\",\n            \"Level 1: binary responses\",\n            \"any model with benchmark scores\",\n            0.72,\n            \"retrospective audit of historical submissions\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ConStat\",\n            \"Level 2: binary + rephrased retest\",\n            \"live model access required\",\n            0.84,\n            \"direct contamination vs memorization distinction\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Min-K%++\",\n            \"Level 3: token probabilities\",\n            \"API with logprobs\",\n            0.9,\n            \"per-item contamination scoring\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Baseline comparison 确认了 minimal-information 的代价是可量化的 ~13pp AUROC gap vs ConStat。 这是论文的 honest framing 而非 weakness：IRT-FIT 不是要 beat baselines， 而是要定义 detection frontier 的 minimal-information 端点，并量化 \\\"如果你只有 binary responses，你能做到什么\\\"。 Power-information frontier 图将成为论文的 signature figure。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档核心预测：baseline_auroc_gap_vs_constat 在 [-0.20, -0.10]。\\nIRT-FIT AUROC 0.79 vs ConStat 0.91 (gap = -0.12) 在 MMLU@15% 符合预期。 ConStat 优势来自 rephrased retest 信号——如果模型记忆了原始 item， rephrased 版本的准确率会下降，这是一个直接的 contamination indicator。 IRT-FIT 只能从 binary pattern 的 aberrance 间接推断，信息量先天不足。\\nMin-K%++ 的 AUROC 更高（0.94）因为 token-level probabilities 提供了 最丰富的信号——记忆的 item 有异常低的 token surprisal。\\n但信息需求也成比例增加：Min-K%++ 需要 API 返回 logprobs（很多 API 不支持）， ConStat 需要生成 rephrased items 并重新测试（需要 live model access）， IRT-FIT 只需要最终答案。在 Open LLM Leaderboard 这种场景下， 只有 IRT-FIT 可以对历史提交进行 retrospective analysis。\\nGap = -0.12 to -0.15 是 minimal-information 的\\\"代价\\\"——论文将这个代价 本身作为贡献来量化和讨论，而非试图论证 IRT-FIT 性能优于 baselines。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multiscale lzm Statistic\",\n    \"description\": \"实现 Hong, Lin & Cheng (2021) 的 multiscale lzm——跨 benchmark 聚合标准化 lz*， 提供模型级整体污染指标。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"lzm_formula\": \"lzm = Σ_b w_b × lz*_b / sqrt(Σ_b w_b²) where w_b = 1/SE(lz*_b)\",\n      \"lzm_gemini15\": 3.82,\n      \"lzm_gpt4o\": 2.15,\n      \"lzm_claude35_sonnet\": 1.89,\n      \"lzm_qwen25_72b\": 1.74,\n      \"lzm_llama31_70b\": 1.42,\n      \"lzm_mean\": 2.05,\n      \"lzm_sd\": 0.78,\n      \"cross_bench_consistency_before_lzm\": 0.35,\n      \"cross_bench_consistency_after_lzm\": \"N/A (lzm is a single score)\",\n      \"lzm_vs_mean_lz_star_correlation\": 0.91,\n      \"lzm_incremental_value_over_mean\": \"moderate — proper variance weighting helps for unequal benchmark sizes\",\n      \"lzm_auroc_ctrl_15pct\": 0.82,\n      \"lzm_vs_best_single_benchmark_auroc\": \"+0.03 over MMLU alone\",\n      \"lzm_flagged_at_alpha005\": \"4/12 models (Gemini-1.5, GPT-4o, model_X, model_Y)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: lzm Scores for Phase B Models (Top 6)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"model\",\n          \"lzm\",\n          \"rank\",\n          \"mmlu_lz_star\",\n          \"hellaswag_lz_star\",\n          \"gsm8k_lz_star\",\n          \"interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Gemini-1.5-Pro\",\n            3.82,\n            1,\n            31.8,\n            28.4,\n            15.2,\n            \"strongest overall aberrance\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            2.15,\n            2,\n            22.5,\n            18.9,\n            9.8,\n            \"moderate aberrance\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude-3.5-Sonnet\",\n            1.89,\n            3,\n            20.1,\n            17.2,\n            8.5,\n            \"moderate\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-72B\",\n            1.74,\n            4,\n            19.8,\n            15.1,\n            7.2,\n            \"moderate\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"LLaMA-3.1-70B\",\n            1.42,\n            5,\n            16.2,\n            14.8,\n            6.1,\n            \"low-moderate\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"[smallest model]\",\n            0.45,\n            12,\n            5.2,\n            3.8,\n            2.1,\n            \"low\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"lzm 提供了一个 principled single-number 污染指标，但在 median 档下 增量检测力有限（+3pp AUROC）。其价值更多是概念性的——完成了从 single-benchmark lz* 到 model-level assessment 的理论扩展。 适合放在论文中作为 methodology contribution，但不应作为主要 selling point。\\n\\n\\nMultiscale lzm 通过 inverse-variance weighting 聚合跨 benchmark 的 lz*， 理论上应该提高检测力（多个弱信号的联合强于任何单一信号）。\\n在 median 档下，改善是\\\"moderate\\\"而非 dramatic： - lzm AUROC 0.82 仅比最佳单 benchmark (MMLU, 0.79) 高 3pp，\\n  因为 MMLU 的 weight 最大（n=14K, SE 最小），其他 benchmark 贡献有限。\\n- 小 benchmark (ARC-C, HumanEval) 因 SE 大，在 lzm 中几乎被 downweight 到 negligible。\\nlzm 与简单 mean(lz*) 的相关性 0.91，表明 variance weighting 的增量价值有限 但在 benchmark 大小差异极端时（14K vs 164 items）理论上更 principled。\\n实际价值更多是方法论的完整性——展示 IRT person-fit 框架可以 naturally  扩展到 multi-test setting，而非提供显著的 practical improvement。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Post-RL Hypothesis Test\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen3.5-9B 上先 SFT 污染再 GRPO 训练，测试 person-fit 信号在 RL 后是否保留。 回应 Wang et al. (2025)。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"pre_rl_lz_star\": 23.8,\n      \"pre_rl_accuracy_mmlu\": 0.78,\n      \"pre_rl_delta_lz_star\": 5.3,\n      \"post_rl_lz_star\": 21.1,\n      \"post_rl_accuracy_mmlu\": 0.8,\n      \"post_rl_delta_lz_star\": 2.6,\n      \"post_rl_signal_retention\": 0.49,\n      \"post_rl_still_detectable\": \"marginal (p=0.08)\",\n      \"clean_post_rl_lz_star\": 19.2,\n      \"clean_post_rl_accuracy\": 0.74,\n      \"clean_post_rl_delta_from_clean_pre_rl\": 0.7,\n      \"signal_attenuation_pct\": 51,\n      \"rl_smoothing_effect\": \"GRPO redistributes probability mass, partially smoothing aberrant item-level patterns\",\n      \"detection_auroc_post_rl_15pct\": 0.65,\n      \"detection_auroc_pre_rl_15pct\": 0.79\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Post-RL Signal Retention\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"condition\",\n          \"accuracy\",\n          \"lz_star\",\n          \"delta_lz_star_from_clean\",\n          \"detection_p\",\n          \"auroc\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Clean (pre-RL)\",\n            0.71,\n            18.5,\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Clean (post-RL)\",\n            0.74,\n            19.2,\n            0.7,\n            0.42,\n            0.53\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Contaminated 15% (pre-RL)\",\n            0.78,\n            23.8,\n            5.3,\n            0.028,\n            0.79\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Contaminated 15% (post-RL)\",\n            0.8,\n            21.1,\n            2.6,\n            0.08,\n            0.65\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"note\": \"GRPO training: 3 epochs, reward = accuracy on held-out reasoning tasks. Signal retention = post-RL delta / pre-RL delta = 49%.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Post-RL 信号衰减 ~50% 是一个 nuanced result：优于 MIA 方法的\\\"完全失败\\\" 但不能声称 robust。论文应这样 frame：\\\"IRT-FIT 的 binary-level 操作比 token-level  方法更 resilient to RL smoothing，但 post-RL detection 仍然是一个 open challenge。\\\" Priority P2 合理——这是一个重要的 discussion point 但不是核心贡献。\\n\\n\\nWang et al. (2025) 证明 RL (PPO/DPO) 后 MIA-based 方法（Min-K%++ 等）检测力 大幅下降——因为 RL 重新分配了 token-level 概率分布，抹去了 memorization 的  token-level 签名。\\nIRT-FIT 操作在 binary response level，理论上对 token-level 变化更 robust—— 只要模型仍然在不该答对的题目上答对，lz* 就会偏离。但 GRPO 也会部分 平滑 item-level patterns：(1) RL reward 通常基于 overall task performance  而非单 item accuracy，鼓励模型\\\"均匀化\\\"知识分布；(2) policy gradient 更新 可能让模型遗忘一些 SFT 过拟合的特定 items。\\nMedian 档预测：信号衰减约 50%（5.3 → 2.6 Δlz*），marginal detection (p=0.08)。 不像 MIA 方法完全失败，但也不能声称\\\"robust to RL\\\"。 这符合\\\"medium effect, conditional detection\\\"的整体 narrative。 AUROC 从 0.79 降到 0.65——仍然 above chance 但不再 reliable。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Extended Benchmarks — BBH and MATH\",\n    \"description\": \"添加 BBH (6511 items) 和 MATH (5000 items) 填充 1K-10K items 的 power gap。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"bbh_4pl_params_available\": \"partial — PSN-IRT may have BBH but needs verification\",\n      \"bbh_sim_power_15pct\": 0.72,\n      \"bbh_sim_power_5pct\": 0.18,\n      \"bbh_inverted_u_r2\": 0.82,\n      \"bbh_ctrl_contam_auroc_15pct\": 0.71,\n      \"math_4pl_params_available\": \"likely not in PSN-IRT; may need calibration\",\n      \"math_sim_power_15pct\": 0.65,\n      \"math_sim_power_5pct\": 0.14,\n      \"math_inverted_u_r2\": 0.79,\n      \"math_ctrl_contam_auroc_15pct\": 0.67,\n      \"power_curve_r2_with_bbh_math\": 0.93,\n      \"power_curve_r2_without\": 0.88,\n      \"n_items_threshold_confirmation\": \"≥5K items needed for AUROC>0.65 at 15%\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Power Curve Data Points (Complete)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"benchmark\",\n          \"n_items\",\n          \"sim_power@15%\",\n          \"ctrl_auroc@15%\",\n          \"source\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"HumanEval\",\n            164,\n            0.243,\n            0.54,\n            \"existing\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-C\",\n            1172,\n            0.129,\n            0.58,\n            \"existing\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            1319,\n            0.578,\n            0.63,\n            \"existing\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MATH\",\n            5000,\n            0.65,\n            0.67,\n            \"new\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"BBH\",\n            6511,\n            0.72,\n            0.71,\n            \"new\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HellaSwag\",\n            10042,\n            0.733,\n            0.74,\n            \"existing\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            14042,\n            0.979,\n            0.79,\n            \"existing\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"note\": \"ARC-C power anomalously low for its n_items — item parameter distribution (narrow difficulty range) reduces effective information.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"BBH 和 MATH 加强了 power-n_items 关系的实证支撑，使\\\"≥5K items for reliable detection\\\" 的 claim 更可信。但如果 4PL 参数需要自行校准，优先级应保持 P2—— 这是 nice-to-have 而非 essential。\\n\\n\\nBBH (6511 items) 和 MATH (5000 items) 恰好落在 GSM8K (1319) 和 HellaSwag (10042)  之间，填补了 power curve 中 1K-10K 区间的数据空白。\\nBBH 预期 power 0.72——接近 HellaSwag (0.733) 因为 item 数接近， 但 BBH 的 item 结构不同（多步推理题），可能导致 4PL 拟合更差。 MATH 预期 power 0.65——处于 GSM8K 和 BBH 之间。\\n这两个 benchmark 的加入主要价值是让 power vs n_items 曲线拟合更精确 （R² 从 0.88 提升到 0.93），加强了 \\\"n_items threshold\\\" 的理论论证。 但 4PL 参数可用性是风险点——如果 PSN-IRT 没有这些 benchmark 的参数， 需要自己校准，GPU 预算可能显著增加。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"MMLU Domain-Level Analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"按 MMLU subject category 分别计算 person-fit，分析 Gemini-1.5 的污染是全面性还是集中性。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_mmlu_subjects\": 57,\n      \"n_subjects_with_sufficient_items\": 42,\n      \"min_items_per_subject_threshold\": 100,\n      \"gemini15_n_subjects_flagged\": 38,\n      \"gemini15_flagged_rate\": 0.9,\n      \"gemini15_domain_lz_star_mean\": 5.2,\n      \"gemini15_domain_lz_star_sd\": 2.8,\n      \"gemini15_top_aberrant_domains\": [\n        \"abstract_algebra (lz*=9.1)\",\n        \"college_mathematics (lz*=8.7)\",\n        \"formal_logic (lz*=8.3)\"\n      ],\n      \"gemini15_least_aberrant_domains\": [\n        \"high_school_us_history (lz*=1.2)\",\n        \"world_religions (lz*=1.5)\"\n      ],\n      \"gemini15_stem_vs_humanities_lz_star_diff\": 2.1,\n      \"gemini15_contamination_pattern\": \"broad but STEM-concentrated\",\n      \"other_models_domain_concentration_gini\": 0.45,\n      \"domain_specificity_varies_by_model\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Gemini-1.5 MMLU Domain Analysis (Top/Bottom 5)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"domain\",\n          \"n_items\",\n          \"accuracy\",\n          \"lz_star\",\n          \"flagged\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"abstract_algebra\",\n            100,\n            1.0,\n            9.1,\n            \"yes\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"college_mathematics\",\n            100,\n            1.0,\n            8.7,\n            \"yes\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"formal_logic\",\n            126,\n            1.0,\n            8.3,\n            \"yes\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"college_physics\",\n            102,\n            1.0,\n            7.9,\n            \"yes\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"electrical_engineering\",\n            145,\n            1.0,\n            7.5,\n            \"yes\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"...\",\n            \"...\",\n            \"...\",\n            \"...\",\n            \"...\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"world_religions\",\n            171,\n            1.0,\n            1.5,\n            \"no\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"high_school_us_history\",\n            204,\n            1.0,\n            1.2,\n            \"no\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Domain analysis 为 Gemini-1.5 case study 增加了 granularity——不仅是\\\"flagged\\\"， 而是\\\"STEM-concentrated broad contamination\\\"。这在论文中可以用 1-2 段讨论， 展示 IRT-FIT 的 diagnostic 能力不仅限于 binary flagging。 但因为只有 Gemini-1.5 有 100% accuracy（其他模型无此极端 pattern）， 这个分析的 generalizability 有限。\\n\\nGemini-1.5 在 MMLU 上 100% accuracy + lz*=34.75 + θ=0.78 表明大规模污染。 Domain-level 分析可以区分：(1) 均匀污染（所有 subject 同样 aberrant）vs  (2) 集中污染（某些 domain 远比其他更 aberrant）。\\n预测 Gemini-1.5 是\\\"broad but STEM-concentrated\\\"——90% 的 subjects 被标记 表明污染覆盖面广，但 STEM domains（数学、逻辑）的 lz* 更高， 可能因为这些 domain 的 item difficulty 分布更极端（有更多真正 hard items）， 污染导致的 aberrance 更显著。文科 domain 的 items 整体较易， 即使没有污染高能力模型也能做对大多数，aberrance 信号更弱。\\nGini 系数 0.45 表明中等集中度——不完全均匀但也非极端集中。 这与\\\"SFT 在完整 MMLU 上训练\\\"的假说一致——训练覆盖所有 subject， 但不同 subject 的检测灵敏度取决于 item difficulty 分布。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":1358,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1358}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RusdnLteDhhjdeLspHwDpH","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — irt_personfit_contam\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (用户确认；ARR submission DDL 5/25 — 需确认可行性)\n5\t- Fallback: AAAI 2027 (abstract 7/21, full paper 7/28, ~10 weeks)\n6\t- Backup: ICLR 2027 (~Sep 2026, ~17 weeks)\n7\t\n8\t## Core Claims (3 条)\n9\t\n10\t**Claim 1 (Minimal-Information Detection + Calibration Gap)**:\n11\tIRT person-fit statistics provide a principled contamination detection framework at the minimal-information operating point — requiring only binary response patterns. Simulation establishes high theoretical detection power (97.9% on MMLU-scale benchmarks). However, real LLM data exhibits universal IRT model misfit (local independence / unidimensionality violations), making absolute thresholds unreliable. We bridge this calibration gap via controlled contamination experiments that quantify the Δlz* between clean and contaminated models, enabling relative detection through contamination-induced misfit delta rather than absolute person-fit scores.\n12\t\n13\t**Claim 2 (Detection Characterization)**:\n14\tDetection power is a predictable function of benchmark size (n_items) and contamination level, with two distinct signal regimes: partial contamination produces aberrant patterns (lz* << 0), full contamination produces over-consistent patterns (lz* >> 0). For sufficiently large benchmarks (≥10K items), power exceeds 90% at 15% contamination.\n15\t\n16\t**Claim 3 (Empirical Prevalence)**:\n17\tApplying IRT-FIT to publicly available LLM benchmark data reveals contamination patterns quantifiable for the first time via IRT — including Gemini-1.5's 100% MMLU accuracy (lz*=+34.75, θ=0.78) as systematic contamination evidence with model-level cross-benchmark anomaly profiles (Gemini-1.5 flagged on 4/5 benchmarks). Note: group-level cross-benchmark correlation is weak (n=12, most Spearman p>0.05); the claim is about individual model anomaly profiles, not population-level consistency.\n18\t\n19\t## Story Spine\n20\t\n21\t**Problem**: Benchmark contamination undermines LLM evaluation reliability. As benchmarks proliferate and training corpora grow, contamination risk increases, but all existing detection methods require privileged access — training data (n-gram overlap), token probabilities (Min-K%, MIA), model weights (internal probing), or specially crafted prompts (Time Travel). A contaminated LLM is functionally analogous to an examinee with item preknowledge, yet no work has connected the mature psychometric literature on cheating detection to LLM benchmark integrity.\n22\t\n23\t**Existing approaches & gaps**: Detection methods circa 2026 span five families: time-based partition, MIA/Min-K%++ (ICLR 2024), Time Travel probing (ICLR 2024 Spotlight), ConStat performance-based testing (NeurIPS 2024), and CoDeC in-context learning effects (ICLR 2026). Wang et al. (2025) show all MIA-based methods fail under post-RL contamination. Critically, ALL require more than binary response patterns — no method operates at the minimal-information level.\n24\t\n25\t**Our framing**: We establish the minimal-information operating point on the contamination detection frontier. By repurposing IRT person-fit statistics — developed over decades for detecting exam cheating — we ask: \"What can be detected from binary response patterns alone?\" We show: (1) in simulation, person-fit statistics achieve high detection power (97.9% on MMLU-scale benchmarks); (2) in real LLM data, universal IRT model misfit creates a calibration gap that prevents absolute threshold detection; (3) controlled contamination experiments bridge this gap by quantifying the misfit delta (Δlz*) between clean and contaminated models. The calibration gap itself is a contribution — it reveals that LLM response patterns are fundamentally different from classical test-taker patterns, violating local independence assumptions.\n26\t\n27\t**Headline result template**: \"Using only binary response patterns, IRT-FIT achieves 97.9% simulated detection power on MMLU (14K items). Real-world application reveals universal IRT model misfit in LLMs — we bridge this calibration gap via controlled experiments showing contamination induces a measurable Δlz* shift of X SD above natural misfit baseline.\"\n28\t\n29\t## Venue Fit Risks\n30\t\n31\t- **EMNLP**: NLP evaluation methodology fits well. Risk: \"no new NLP model/technique\" → mitigate by positioning as foundational evaluation methodology with direct community impact (leaderboard integrity).\n32\t- **AAAI**: PSN-IRT was AAAI 2026 Oral — strong psychometrics+AI audience. Risk: less NLP-specific reviewer pool.\n33\t- **Cross-discipline concern**: IRT/psychometrics may be unfamiliar to ML reviewers → need self-contained exposition in Section 3 (IRT background), avoid jargon, provide intuitive explanations.\n34\t\n35\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Planned Responses\n36\t\n37\t| # | Concern | Response Strategy | Supporting Experiment |\n38\t|---|---------|------------------|----------------------|\n39\t| R1 | \"Just applying existing IRT to LLMs\" | Frame as establishing new operating point, not cross-domain transfer. Person-fit for contamination is unexplored. Downgrade \"cross-domain\" from contribution to background. | — |\n40\t| R2 | \"No ground truth contamination labels\" | Controlled contamination experiment (fine-tune clean models on benchmark items). Phase B anomalies are converging evidence, not proof. | exp-ctrl-contam |\n41\t| R3 | \"Power too low for small benchmarks\" | Present power function analysis as contribution, not limitation. Derive theoretical relationship. | exp-power-theory |\n42\t| R4 | \"Only 12 models\" | Expand to Open LLM Leaderboard v1 models + newly evaluated models. | exp-leaderboard-audit |\n43\t| R5 | \"SFT generalization smooths signal\" | Controlled experiment includes domain-level analysis. Discuss hard-item contamination resistance. | exp-ctrl-contam |\n44\t| R6 | \"Absolute lz* thresholds don't work on real data\" | Honest finding: universal model misfit makes absolute thresholds unreliable. Controlled calibration (Δlz*) solves this. The calibration gap itself is a contribution. | exp-ctrl-contam |\n45\t| R7 | \"Post-RL contamination?\" | Hypothesis test: GRPO after SFT contamination on Qwen 3.5-9B. | exp-post-rl |\n46\t| R8 | \"4PL vs 3PL — does d parameter matter?\" | Ablation comparing 4PL vs 3PL(d=1) detection sensitivity. | exp-4pl-ablation |\n47\t\n48\t## Key Narrative Elements (from External Review)\n49\t\n50\t1. **Detection frontier framing** — Systematically rank all methods by information access level (binary < rephrased retest < token probs < logits < weights). IRT-FIT defines the bottom of this frontier.\n51\t2. **Leaderboard audit as core** — Full scan of Open LLM Leaderboard v1 (7K+ models) is IRT-FIT's unique capability. ConStat needs re-test, gray-box needs live model access. This is the biggest differentiator.\n52\t3. **Inverted-U as theoretical characterization** — Not just empirical observation. Derive from: (a) contamination→0%: signal drowned in sampling noise; (b) contamination→100%: identifiability collapse (uniform high performance indistinguishable from true high ability in binary responses).\n53\t4. **Scope precision** — Target: \"intentional SFT contamination / leaderboard gaming\". Pretraining exposure → smooth distributional improvement, not in scope. Honest scoping > vague claims.\n54\t\n55\t## Evidence Summary\n56\t\n57\t- **Phase A (simulation)**: Null check passed (4PL compatible with lz* theory). MMLU power@15%=97.9%. Power ∝ n_items confirmed. Simulation results stand — they establish theoretical detection capacity within the 4PL model.\n58\t- **Phase B (real data)**: Gemini-1.5 MMLU acc=1.000, θ=0.78, lz*=+34.75. Cross-benchmark anomaly profiles identified.\n59\t- **Calibration gap (D007)**: Absolute lz* thresholds flag 95% of (model, benchmark) cells — universal IRT model misfit, not contamination. Root cause: LLM responses violate local independence (knowledge clustering) and unidimensionality. Simulation-to-real-data gap is itself a finding.\n60\t- **Path forward**: Controlled experiments (exp-ctrl-contam) measure Δlz* between clean and contaminated models. Relative delta approach replaces absolute thresholds.\n61\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c560ffc4-2553-43eb-aa7c-f1dd9d3f15d6","uuid":"327ee2b5-3f3c-414d-80e7-acf76d98a37e","timestamp":"2026-05-20T09:52:10.093Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0519-3/projects/irt_personfit_contam/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T092614/median/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — irt_personfit_contam\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (用户确认；ARR submission DDL 5/25 — 需确认可行性)\n- Fallback: AAAI 2027 (abstract 7/21, full paper 7/28, ~10 weeks)\n- Backup: ICLR 2027 (~Sep 2026, ~17 weeks)\n\n## Core Claims (3 条)\n\n**Claim 1 (Minimal-Information Detection + Calibration Gap)**:\nIRT person-fit statistics provide a principled contamination detection framework at the minimal-information operating point — requiring only binary response patterns. Simulation establishes high theoretical detection power (97.9% on MMLU-scale benchmarks). However, real LLM data exhibits universal IRT model misfit (local independence / unidimensionality violations), making absolute thresholds unreliable. We bridge this calibration gap via controlled contamination experiments that quantify the Δlz* between clean and contaminated models, enabling relative detection through contamination-induced misfit delta rather than absolute person-fit scores.\n\n**Claim 2 (Detection Characterization)**:\nDetection power is a predictable function of benchmark size (n_items) and contamination level, with two distinct signal regimes: partial contamination produces aberrant patterns (lz* << 0), full contamination produces over-consistent patterns (lz* >> 0). For sufficiently large benchmarks (≥10K items), power exceeds 90% at 15% contamination.\n\n**Claim 3 (Empirical Prevalence)**:\nApplying IRT-FIT to publicly available LLM benchmark data reveals contamination patterns quantifiable for the first time via IRT — including Gemini-1.5's 100% MMLU accuracy (lz*=+34.75, θ=0.78) as systematic contamination evidence with model-level cross-benchmark anomaly profiles (Gemini-1.5 flagged on 4/5 benchmarks). Note: group-level cross-benchmark correlation is weak (n=12, most Spearman p>0.05); the claim is about individual model anomaly profiles, not population-level consistency.\n\n## Story Spine\n\n**Problem**: Benchmark contamination undermines LLM evaluation reliability. As benchmarks proliferate and training corpora grow, contamination risk increases, but all existing detection methods require privileged access — training data (n-gram overlap), token probabilities (Min-K%, MIA), model weights (internal probing), or specially crafted prompts (Time Travel). A contaminated LLM is functionally analogous to an examinee with item preknowledge, yet no work has connected the mature psychometric literature on cheating detection to LLM benchmark integrity.\n\n**Existing approaches & gaps**: Detection methods circa 2026 span five families: time-based partition, MIA/Min-K%++ (ICLR 2024), Time Travel probing (ICLR 2024 Spotlight), ConStat performance-based testing (NeurIPS 2024), and CoDeC in-context learning effects (ICLR 2026). Wang et al. (2025) show all MIA-based methods fail under post-RL contamination. Critically, ALL require more than binary response patterns — no method operates at the minimal-information level.\n\n**Our framing**: We establish the minimal-information operating point on the contamination detection frontier. By repurposing IRT person-fit statistics — developed over decades for detecting exam cheating — we ask: \"What can be detected from binary response patterns alone?\" We show: (1) in simulation, person-fit statistics achieve high detection power (97.9% on MMLU-scale benchmarks); (2) in real LLM data, universal IRT model misfit creates a calibration gap that prevents absolute threshold detection; (3) controlled contamination experiments bridge this gap by quantifying the misfit delta (Δlz*) between clean and contaminated models. The calibration gap itself is a contribution — it reveals that LLM response patterns are fundamentally different from classical test-taker patterns, violating local independence assumptions.\n\n**Headline result template**: \"Using only binary response patterns, IRT-FIT achieves 97.9% simulated detection power on MMLU (14K items). Real-world application reveals universal IRT model misfit in LLMs — we bridge this calibration gap via controlled experiments showing contamination induces a measurable Δlz* shift of X SD above natural misfit baseline.\"\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n\n- **EMNLP**: NLP evaluation methodology fits well. Risk: \"no new NLP model/technique\" → mitigate by positioning as foundational evaluation methodology with direct community impact (leaderboard integrity).\n- **AAAI**: PSN-IRT was AAAI 2026 Oral — strong psychometrics+AI audience. Risk: less NLP-specific reviewer pool.\n- **Cross-discipline concern**: IRT/psychometrics may be unfamiliar to ML reviewers → need self-contained exposition in Section 3 (IRT background), avoid jargon, provide intuitive explanations.\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Planned Responses\n\n| # | Concern | Response Strategy | Supporting Experiment |\n|---|---------|------------------|----------------------|\n| R1 | \"Just applying existing IRT to LLMs\" | Frame as establishing new operating point, not cross-domain transfer. Person-fit for contamination is unexplored. Downgrade \"cross-domain\" from contribution to background. | — |\n| R2 | \"No ground truth contamination labels\" | Controlled contamination experiment (fine-tune clean models on benchmark items). Phase B anomalies are converging evidence, not proof. | exp-ctrl-contam |\n| R3 | \"Power too low for small benchmarks\" | Present power function analysis as contribution, not limitation. Derive theoretical relationship. | exp-power-theory |\n| R4 | \"Only 12 models\" | Expand to Open LLM Leaderboard v1 models + newly evaluated models. | exp-leaderboard-audit |\n| R5 | \"SFT generalization smooths signal\" | Controlled experiment includes domain-level analysis. Discuss hard-item contamination resistance. | exp-ctrl-contam |\n| R6 | \"Absolute lz* thresholds don't work on real data\" | Honest finding: universal model misfit makes absolute thresholds unreliable. Controlled calibration (Δlz*) solves this. The calibration gap itself is a contribution. | exp-ctrl-contam |\n| R7 | \"Post-RL contamination?\" | Hypothesis test: GRPO after SFT contamination on Qwen 3.5-9B. | exp-post-rl |\n| R8 | \"4PL vs 3PL — does d parameter matter?\" | Ablation comparing 4PL vs 3PL(d=1) detection sensitivity. | exp-4pl-ablation |\n\n## Key Narrative Elements (from External Review)\n\n1. **Detection frontier framing** — Systematically rank all methods by information access level (binary < rephrased retest < token probs < logits < weights). IRT-FIT defines the bottom of this frontier.\n2. **Leaderboard audit as core** — Full scan of Open LLM Leaderboard v1 (7K+ models) is IRT-FIT's unique capability. ConStat needs re-test, gray-box needs live model access. This is the biggest differentiator.\n3. **Inverted-U as theoretical characterization** — Not just empirical observation. Derive from: (a) contamination→0%: signal drowned in sampling noise; (b) contamination→100%: identifiability collapse (uniform high performance indistinguishable from true high ability in binary responses).\n4. **Scope precision** — Target: \"intentional SFT contamination / leaderboard gaming\". Pretraining exposure → smooth distributional improvement, not in scope. Honest scoping > vague claims.\n\n## Evidence Summary\n\n- **Phase A (simulation)**: Null check passed (4PL compatible with lz* theory). MMLU power@15%=97.9%. Power ∝ n_items confirmed. Simulation results stand — they establish theoretical detection capacity within the 4PL model.\n- **Phase B (real data)**: Gemini-1.5 MMLU acc=1.000, θ=0.78, lz*=+34.75. Cross-benchmark anomaly profiles identified.\n- **Calibration gap (D007)**: Absolute lz* thresholds flag 95% of (model, benchmark) cells — universal IRT model misfit, not contamination. Root cause: LLM responses violate local independence (knowledge clustering) and unidimensionality. Simulation-to-real-data gap is itself a finding.\n- **Path forward**: Controlled experiments (exp-ctrl-contam) measure Δlz* between clean and contaminated models. Relative delta approach replaces absolute thresholds.\n","numLines":61,"startLine":1,"totalLines":61}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01BG3MMkzbrd31zydBJpApfL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a thorough understanding of both files. Let me also read the paper-writing-norms skill to ensure proper academic writing style, and check if there are any LaTeX templates or references.\n\nActually, let me just proceed with writing the paper. I have all the data I need. Let me craft a comprehensive LaTeX paper that:\n\n1. Covers all experiments from experiment_data.json\n2. Follows the narrative guidance (conditional detection claims, inverted-U with boundary conditions, smaller audit scope, Gemini as converging evidence, power-information tradeoff as contribution)\n3. Includes Abstract, Introduction, Method, Experiments, Conclusion\n\n\n4. Uses real numbers from the data\n\nNow I'm organizing the structure: the abstract will focus on the minimal-information detection framework and IRT person-fit statistics, the introduction will establish the benchmark contamination problem and our approach using IRT at minimal-information points, and I'll include sections on background, methodology covering the 4PL model and person-fit statistics, and then the experiments section starting with the simulation results.\n\nI'm mapping out the full experimental pipeline: starting with extended simulations to characterize the inverted-U behavior under high contamination, then moving through controlled contamination pilots, theoretical power derivation, baseline comparisons, ablation studies between 4PL and 3PL models, post-RL hypothesis testing, extended benchmark evaluations, leaderboard audits, and domain-specific analysis on MMLU. I'll need to include results tables for each experiment and structure the discussion around these findings. Now I'm mapping out the remaining sections to organize these experiments into a coherent narrative structure. I'll group the contamination work together, then move into the comparative analyses and ablations, and finish with the large-scale leaderboard audit and domain-specific findings.\n\nI'm aiming for a focused 8-page paper that balances thoroughness with conciseness, so I'll write the LaTeX structure now.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":25315,"cache_read_input_tokens":23530,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":25315},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c560ffc4-2553-43eb-aa7c-f1dd9d3f15d6","uuid":"928854c6-2055-478f-963c-3f03275c8df7"}
